1
00:00:41,834 --> 00:00:42,668
[Snake] Stop.

2
00:00:42,751 --> 00:00:44,753
[Wolf] I'll stop if you just
explain it to me, because I don't…

3
00:00:44,837 --> 00:00:46,129
[Snake] Would you please
just drop it?

4
00:00:46,213 --> 00:00:47,506
[Wolf] All right, all right.
Fine, fine, fine.

5
00:00:47,589 --> 00:00:49,299
Consider it dropped.
It's dropped. It's on the ground.

6
00:00:49,383 --> 00:00:50,259
Good.

7
00:00:52,010 --> 00:00:54,096
But, I mean, come on,
everybody loves birthdays.

8
00:00:54,179 --> 00:00:55,013
[groans]

9
00:00:55,097 --> 00:00:56,473
You got decorations,
you got balloons,

10
00:00:56,557 --> 00:00:57,808
you got parties and cake.

11
00:00:57,891 --> 00:01:00,769
Look. I don't need presents,
I don't want decorations,

12
00:01:00,853 --> 00:01:02,479
and I'm not a cake guy.

13
00:01:02,563 --> 00:01:04,647
Seriously, though,
you don't like cake?

14
00:01:04,730 --> 00:01:06,817
Name one food
better than cake.

15
00:01:06,900 --> 00:01:07,985
Guinea pig.

16
00:01:08,068 --> 00:01:09,611
Again, with the guinea pig.

17
00:01:09,695 --> 00:01:11,613
[chuckles]
I bet if I blindfolded you,

18
00:01:11,697 --> 00:01:13,031
you wouldn't be able to tell

19
00:01:13,115 --> 00:01:15,450
the difference between
a skunk and a guinea pig.

20
00:01:15,534 --> 00:01:16,618
Wrong.

21
00:01:16,702 --> 00:01:19,955
Snakes have impeccable taste buds.
I can taste air.

22
00:01:20,038 --> 00:01:21,999
-Air?
-Yes. Air.

23
00:01:22,082 --> 00:01:24,251
[lapping] Mmm.

24
00:01:24,334 --> 00:01:25,377
Nice.

25
00:01:25,460 --> 00:01:27,629
I don't know.
They're a little, uh…

26
00:01:27,713 --> 00:01:29,047
They're a little cute
for my taste.

27
00:01:29,131 --> 00:01:31,425
That's what makes them
so delicious.

28
00:01:31,508 --> 00:01:35,012
You're not just eating food,
you're eating pure goodness.

29
00:01:35,095 --> 00:01:36,680
It's not about the pig.

30
00:01:36,763 --> 00:01:39,892
It's about what it symbolizes
on a deeper level.

31
00:01:41,435 --> 00:01:43,020
So, you can…
You can taste air?

32
00:01:43,103 --> 00:01:44,897
-Ah. Forget about it.
-What else you got?

33
00:01:44,980 --> 00:01:46,940
Wait, wait, wait.
Can you also hear color?

34
00:01:47,024 --> 00:01:48,317
-[laughing]
-All right, all right.

35
00:01:48,400 --> 00:01:49,443
-Can you see sound?
-Okay.

36
00:01:49,526 --> 00:01:51,361
'Cause we should really be
capitalizing on these skills.

37
00:01:51,445 --> 00:01:52,613
Okay, all right, fine.

38
00:01:52,696 --> 00:01:54,948
-Get it all out. Get it all out now.
-Okay, okay.

39
00:01:55,032 --> 00:01:56,283
[gags]

40
00:01:56,366 --> 00:01:58,035
Look at that. 4:00 p.m.

41
00:01:58,118 --> 00:02:00,621
Now I know the exact moment
our friendship died.

42
00:02:00,704 --> 00:02:02,581
[laughs]

43
00:02:02,664 --> 00:02:04,166
-Let's bounce.
-Yep.

44
00:02:05,501 --> 00:02:08,961
Tastes like, uh, you're gonna
stick me with the bill… again.

45
00:02:09,045 --> 00:02:10,839
-Well, it is my birthday.
-[patrons gasp, shudder]

46
00:02:10,923 --> 00:02:13,467
So, now you play the birthday card?
That's interesting.

47
00:02:13,550 --> 00:02:14,843
[laughs]

48
00:02:14,927 --> 00:02:17,012
Can we get a check, please,
when you get a chance?

49
00:02:17,930 --> 00:02:20,098
Hello?
Checkity-check-check.

50
00:02:20,974 --> 00:02:22,100
You know what?

51
00:02:22,184 --> 00:02:25,270
We're just gonna leave
the money right here, okay?

52
00:02:25,896 --> 00:02:27,689
You know the one good thing
about this place?

53
00:02:27,773 --> 00:02:29,900
-What?
-We never have to wait for a table.

54
00:02:29,983 --> 00:02:31,193
Well, isn't that every place?

55
00:02:31,276 --> 00:02:32,903
Hey, man. How you been?
I haven't seen you…

56
00:02:32,986 --> 00:02:34,821
-Snake attack! [laughs]
-[patrons gasping]

57
00:02:34,905 --> 00:02:36,490
Oh! Mints.

58
00:02:36,573 --> 00:02:38,659
Sorry, folks.
I'm switching him to decaf.

59
00:02:38,742 --> 00:02:40,244
[laughs]

60
00:02:40,327 --> 00:02:42,329
-All right.
-[both] Let's do this.

61
00:02:42,955 --> 00:02:46,542
-[pedestrians screaming]
-[tires screeching]

62
00:02:47,209 --> 00:02:49,878
-[screaming continues]
-[crashing]

63
00:02:56,385 --> 00:02:57,427
Guinea pig, huh?

64
00:02:57,511 --> 00:02:59,263
It's the Rolls Royce of rodents.

65
00:02:59,346 --> 00:03:01,974
Yeah, but it's still a rodent.
You know what I mean?

66
00:03:03,350 --> 00:03:05,519
Don't mind us,
just robbin' this place.

67
00:03:05,602 --> 00:03:07,187
[people screaming]

68
00:03:07,271 --> 00:03:09,773
-[glass shattering]
-[alarm blaring]

69
00:03:16,697 --> 00:03:18,407
[tires squealing]

70
00:03:18,490 --> 00:03:22,160
-Whoo! Yeah! Go bad…
-Or go home.

71
00:03:22,244 --> 00:03:23,245
[both laughing]

72
00:03:23,328 --> 00:03:25,289
[engine revs]

73
00:03:27,875 --> 00:03:30,377
Hey, you. Get over here.

74
00:03:30,919 --> 00:03:32,379
Little bit closer.

75
00:03:33,297 --> 00:03:35,716
Oh, I know what it is.

76
00:03:35,799 --> 00:03:39,553
You're afraid.
Because I'm the big, bad wolf.

77
00:03:40,137 --> 00:03:43,182
Well, I'm not surprised.
I am the villain in every story.

78
00:03:43,265 --> 00:03:45,976
-Isn't that right, Mr. Snake?
-[laughs] Yep.

79
00:03:46,059 --> 00:03:48,395
Say hello to Mr. Snake.

80
00:03:49,188 --> 00:03:51,190
Serpentine, safecrackin' machine.

81
00:03:51,273 --> 00:03:53,317
Imagine Houdini, but with no arms.

82
00:03:53,400 --> 00:03:56,737
Kinda guy who'd tell ya the glass
is half empty, then steal it from ya.

83
00:03:56,820 --> 00:04:00,657
He's also my best bud,
and today's his birthday!

84
00:04:00,741 --> 00:04:01,867
Not relevant.

85
00:04:01,950 --> 00:04:04,203
He's a sweetheart.
You're a sweetheart.

86
00:04:04,286 --> 00:04:05,287
[siren wailing]

87
00:04:05,370 --> 00:04:06,747
Well, look who's here.

88
00:04:06,830 --> 00:04:07,956
Took 'em long enough.

89
00:04:13,545 --> 00:04:14,755
Watch this.

90
00:04:16,214 --> 00:04:18,509
Three… Two…

91
00:04:18,591 --> 00:04:19,635
One.

92
00:04:20,135 --> 00:04:22,721
And over here is Ms. Tarantula.

93
00:04:22,804 --> 00:04:25,057
Our in-house hacker,
pocket search engine,

94
00:04:25,140 --> 00:04:26,558
our traveling tech wizard.

95
00:04:26,642 --> 00:04:28,185
We call her "Webs."

96
00:04:32,773 --> 00:04:34,358
-[siren blaring]
-[horns honking]

97
00:04:34,441 --> 00:04:35,442
Very slick, Webs.

98
00:04:35,526 --> 00:04:37,194
I also took over the police dispatch,

99
00:04:37,277 --> 00:04:38,862
blurred their
satellite imaging system,

100
00:04:38,946 --> 00:04:41,823
grounded their chopper,
and one more thing…

101
00:04:41,907 --> 00:04:43,033
You didn't.

102
00:04:43,116 --> 00:04:44,743
I got a special delivery for…

103
00:04:44,826 --> 00:04:48,038
[screams] Whoa, don't eat me!
Please, don't eat me!

104
00:04:48,121 --> 00:04:50,832
Happy birthday,
Mr. Grumpypants.

105
00:04:50,916 --> 00:04:52,543
I think I hate you.

106
00:05:02,553 --> 00:05:03,679
-Ooh!
-Oh!

107
00:05:06,557 --> 00:05:08,058
Guys! It's me!

108
00:05:08,141 --> 00:05:09,476
I was the construction worker!

109
00:05:09,560 --> 00:05:13,355
[Wolf] And this is Mr. Shark,
master of disguise.

110
00:05:13,438 --> 00:05:16,024
Apex predator of a thousand faces.

111
00:05:16,900 --> 00:05:18,193
His greatest trick?

112
00:05:18,277 --> 00:05:21,822
Stealing the Mona Lisa,
disguised as the Mona Lisa.

113
00:05:21,905 --> 00:05:23,073
Dig that.

114
00:05:23,156 --> 00:05:25,951
Watch it, big tuna.
I'm tryin' to work here.

115
00:05:26,034 --> 00:05:29,162
Keep it cool, baby.
Birthdays should be chill.

116
00:05:30,122 --> 00:05:32,624
[Wolf] And rounding out the crew…

117
00:05:32,708 --> 00:05:34,168
[knocking]

118
00:05:34,251 --> 00:05:37,004
Surprise! [cackling]

119
00:05:37,087 --> 00:05:39,339
[Wolf] …is Mr. Piranha.

120
00:05:39,423 --> 00:05:40,841
-He's a loose cannon…
-[thugs laughing]

121
00:05:40,924 --> 00:05:43,844
…with a short fuse, willing to scrap
with anyone or anything.

122
00:05:43,927 --> 00:05:45,095
He's brave.

123
00:05:46,096 --> 00:05:47,931
-He's fearless.
-[thugs screaming]

124
00:05:48,015 --> 00:05:50,100
Uh, who am I kidding? He's crazy.

125
00:05:50,184 --> 00:05:53,270
[laughing, speaking Spanish]

126
00:05:53,353 --> 00:05:56,565
Uh, Piranha,
did we forget something?

127
00:05:56,648 --> 00:05:59,276
-What?
-The present. You know?

128
00:05:59,359 --> 00:06:01,862
Oh, um, of course I didn't forget.

129
00:06:01,945 --> 00:06:03,238
[siren wailing continues]

130
00:06:03,322 --> 00:06:04,948
You know you fart
when you lie, right?

131
00:06:05,032 --> 00:06:06,742
What? No, I fart when I'm nervous.

132
00:06:06,825 --> 00:06:08,869
-Yeah. Nervous about lying.
-[stomach gurgling]

133
00:06:08,952 --> 00:06:09,953
I'm sorry.

134
00:06:10,037 --> 00:06:11,788
-[farts]
-[Tarantula] Piranha!

135
00:06:11,872 --> 00:06:13,624
Don't breathe it in.
I breathed it in!

136
00:06:13,707 --> 00:06:14,708
[Wolf, Snake gasp]

137
00:06:14,791 --> 00:06:17,044
[Wolf] Yeah, they're a bit eccentric,
but when you're born us,

138
00:06:17,127 --> 00:06:19,755
you don't exactly win
many popularity contests.

139
00:06:19,838 --> 00:06:20,839
Shark!

140
00:06:20,923 --> 00:06:22,341
-[beachgoer] A shark!
-[screaming]

141
00:06:22,424 --> 00:06:24,843
Do I wish people
didn't see us as monsters?

142
00:06:24,927 --> 00:06:26,136
Eight legs, eight times the cardio!

143
00:06:26,220 --> 00:06:28,096
-Spider!
-[Wolf] Sure, I do.

144
00:06:28,180 --> 00:06:29,223
What's up, papa?

145
00:06:29,306 --> 00:06:31,934
But these are the cards we've been
dealt, so we might as well play them.

146
00:06:32,017 --> 00:06:33,560
-[lock clicks]
-Jackpot!

147
00:06:33,644 --> 00:06:34,645
Yes!

148
00:06:36,230 --> 00:06:38,273
[tires screeching]

149
00:06:44,947 --> 00:06:46,031
Um…

150
00:06:46,907 --> 00:06:48,534
-What the thorax?
-Are you crazy?

151
00:06:48,617 --> 00:06:51,161
What? I just wanted
a longer car chase.

152
00:06:51,245 --> 00:06:52,579
It's the best part.

153
00:06:54,248 --> 00:06:55,582
[police radio chatter]

154
00:06:55,666 --> 00:06:57,042
Chief! It's…

155
00:06:57,876 --> 00:06:58,794
Them.

156
00:06:58,877 --> 00:07:00,045
[grunts]

157
00:07:00,128 --> 00:07:01,922
Webs, hit it.

158
00:07:02,005 --> 00:07:04,675
["Stop, Drop, Roll" plays on radio]

159
00:07:04,758 --> 00:07:06,301
Get them!

160
00:07:06,385 --> 00:07:08,095
-[all laughing]
-[engine revs]

161
00:07:13,517 --> 00:07:15,519
-[officers clamoring]
-[sirens wailing]

162
00:07:19,398 --> 00:07:22,359
♪ Hooked on hip-hop phonics
Yeah it works for me ♪

163
00:07:22,442 --> 00:07:24,862
♪ So jump aboard
Yeah, this train is free ♪

164
00:07:24,945 --> 00:07:27,281
♪ The conductor let me
Toot my whistle ♪

165
00:07:27,364 --> 00:07:30,117
♪ The instructor
Of the funky uncle fizzle ♪

166
00:07:30,200 --> 00:07:32,202
♪ We be dancing on a lake
When it ain't froze over ♪

167
00:07:32,286 --> 00:07:34,496
♪ We be walking on water
While you're sinking your rover ♪

168
00:07:34,580 --> 00:07:36,707
♪ If you step any close
You'll be eatin' some teeth ♪

169
00:07:38,292 --> 00:07:40,210
[cackling]

170
00:07:40,294 --> 00:07:42,629
I'm gonna put you guys away
for so long,

171
00:07:42,713 --> 00:07:44,381
your fleas will have fleas!

172
00:07:45,382 --> 00:07:46,508
[Chief grunts]

173
00:07:46,592 --> 00:07:47,843
[all gasp]

174
00:07:49,428 --> 00:07:50,846
Chief! You want some cake?

175
00:07:50,929 --> 00:07:53,640
-You seem a little hangry.
-[all laughing]

176
00:07:53,724 --> 00:07:55,851
Get that thing
out of my face before I…

177
00:07:55,934 --> 00:07:57,436
-Excuse me, Chief.
-What?

178
00:08:07,321 --> 00:08:08,864
[siren wailing continues]

179
00:08:12,075 --> 00:08:13,368
You're mine.

180
00:08:14,578 --> 00:08:15,954
[engine revs]

181
00:08:19,166 --> 00:08:20,167
Hermano!

182
00:08:23,670 --> 00:08:25,047
[tires squealing]

183
00:08:26,882 --> 00:08:27,925
[Wolf] Whoo!

184
00:08:28,008 --> 00:08:30,219
[all screaming]

185
00:08:48,570 --> 00:08:52,741
Yeah. We may be bad,
but we're so good at it.

186
00:08:52,824 --> 00:08:54,451
[all laughing]

187
00:08:59,498 --> 00:09:01,625
No, no, no, no, no!

188
00:09:01,708 --> 00:09:04,127
No, no! Keep runnin', Wolf.

189
00:09:04,211 --> 00:09:07,172
One of these days
your luck is gonna run out.

190
00:09:29,653 --> 00:09:31,071
[elevator bell dings]

191
00:09:36,618 --> 00:09:39,288
All right, Piranha. You're up.

192
00:09:39,371 --> 00:09:43,709
[vocalizing]

193
00:09:43,792 --> 00:09:45,294
Happy birth…

194
00:09:45,919 --> 00:09:47,212
-[gasps]
-Seriously?

195
00:09:47,296 --> 00:09:49,173
Snake, come on.
At least make a toast.

196
00:09:49,840 --> 00:09:50,966
-Toast.
-Come on.

197
00:09:51,049 --> 00:09:52,718
-Okay, all right, a toast.
-Yeah!

198
00:09:52,801 --> 00:09:53,886
Fine.

199
00:09:53,969 --> 00:09:55,929
I've made a lot of enemies
in my time.

200
00:09:56,013 --> 00:09:57,472
I mean, a lot!

201
00:09:57,556 --> 00:09:59,600
But out of all the people
in the world,

202
00:10:00,726 --> 00:10:02,561
I hate you guys the least.

203
00:10:02,644 --> 00:10:04,229
That was actually
kind of beautiful.

204
00:10:04,313 --> 00:10:05,314
You a poet, man.

205
00:10:05,397 --> 00:10:09,568
To Mr. Snake
and his strange dislike of birthdays.

206
00:10:09,651 --> 00:10:11,945
[all cheering]

207
00:10:12,029 --> 00:10:14,656
Everyone say, "Robbery!"

208
00:10:14,740 --> 00:10:16,533
[all] Robbery!

209
00:10:17,492 --> 00:10:19,578
Look at those dimples.

210
00:10:19,661 --> 00:10:20,913
Happy birthday, buddy.

211
00:10:20,996 --> 00:10:22,581
Okay. Now, dig in, fellas.

212
00:10:22,664 --> 00:10:23,874
Yes! [laughs]

213
00:10:23,957 --> 00:10:25,459
-No, no, no!
-Piranha!

214
00:10:26,043 --> 00:10:28,170
-[Wolf] Don't do that.
-[Tarantula] That was so gross.

215
00:10:28,253 --> 00:10:29,755
[Shark] That was my lunch.

216
00:10:29,838 --> 00:10:31,924
-[Piranha] You snooze, you lose.
-[Tarantula laughing]

217
00:10:32,007 --> 00:10:33,258
[Wolf] You like that.

218
00:10:34,676 --> 00:10:35,677
Nice.

219
00:10:37,054 --> 00:10:38,639
-Ooh! Wow!
-[Snake gasps]

220
00:10:38,722 --> 00:10:40,432
I forgot we had those Push Pops.

221
00:10:40,516 --> 00:10:43,185
Man, my tummy is rumblin'
like a kraken right now.

222
00:10:43,268 --> 00:10:44,978
Yeah. Want it?

223
00:10:45,062 --> 00:10:47,231
You know he's not
gonna give it to you.

224
00:10:47,314 --> 00:10:51,610
No. I believe that, deep down,
Snake is a kind and generous soul.

225
00:10:52,653 --> 00:10:53,737
Why?

226
00:10:53,820 --> 00:10:55,906
Here. Take it.

227
00:10:55,989 --> 00:10:58,408
Oh, yeah! Pop me, please.

228
00:11:00,661 --> 00:11:01,662
[gasps, sighs]

229
00:11:01,745 --> 00:11:03,539
-[laughs] Sucker.
-Come on, man!

230
00:11:03,622 --> 00:11:05,541
Now you're gonna make me
get all aggressive.

231
00:11:07,626 --> 00:11:10,087
-Animals.
-Spit it out! Spit it out!

232
00:11:10,170 --> 00:11:11,255
[Snake] Never!

233
00:11:11,338 --> 00:11:13,048
Let's see
what they're sayin' about us today.

234
00:11:13,131 --> 00:11:16,468
What up? It's Tiffany Fluffit,
Channel 6 Action News.

235
00:11:16,552 --> 00:11:17,761
The Bad Guys have struck again…

236
00:11:17,845 --> 00:11:20,305
-Guys, stop it. We're on TV.
-…with their most brazen heist yet,

237
00:11:20,389 --> 00:11:23,976
proving once more that they are
the most diabolical criminals

238
00:11:24,059 --> 00:11:25,352
of our time.

239
00:11:25,435 --> 00:11:27,312
"Diabolical." That's new.

240
00:11:27,396 --> 00:11:29,273
Know what it sounds like? A cologne.

241
00:11:29,356 --> 00:11:30,274
"Diabolical."

242
00:11:30,357 --> 00:11:32,234
To address this heinous crime spree

243
00:11:32,317 --> 00:11:35,362
is the newly elected governor,
Diane Foxington.

244
00:11:35,445 --> 00:11:36,864
-Governor?
-[Diane] Okay, yeah.

245
00:11:36,947 --> 00:11:38,240
I hear you. I hear you.

246
00:11:38,323 --> 00:11:39,449
Listen, listen.

247
00:11:39,533 --> 00:11:42,202
We all know
how dastardly the Bad Guys are.

248
00:11:42,286 --> 00:11:43,495
You bet we are.

249
00:11:43,579 --> 00:11:46,623
But more than anything…
[chuckles]

250
00:11:46,707 --> 00:11:47,958
…I feel sorry for them.

251
00:11:48,041 --> 00:11:49,084
What?

252
00:11:49,751 --> 00:11:54,298
These so-called "Bad Guys" are
really just second-rate has-beens.

253
00:11:54,381 --> 00:11:58,677
Behind their amateurish antics
and, frankly, unoriginal capers…

254
00:11:58,760 --> 00:12:00,637
I mean, really? Another bank?

255
00:12:00,721 --> 00:12:02,890
…is nothing but a deep well of anger.

256
00:12:02,973 --> 00:12:04,391
I ain't angry! You're angry!

257
00:12:04,474 --> 00:12:06,101
-Denial.
-Not true.

258
00:12:06,185 --> 00:12:07,269
And self-loathing.

259
00:12:07,352 --> 00:12:09,605
The only one I self-loathe is you.

260
00:12:09,688 --> 00:12:14,818
And those are holes that no amount of
cash or priceless art can ever fill.

261
00:12:17,279 --> 00:12:19,323
What's on the Food Network?

262
00:12:19,406 --> 00:12:21,283
Can we just forget about
the Bad Guys…

263
00:12:21,366 --> 00:12:22,784
Who is she to judge us?

264
00:12:22,868 --> 00:12:24,620
-…and focus on more positive things?
-[growls]

265
00:12:24,703 --> 00:12:28,332
And what could be more positive than
the Annual Good Samaritan Awards,

266
00:12:28,415 --> 00:12:30,334
where tomorrow night I will present

267
00:12:30,417 --> 00:12:34,213
the Golden Dolphin
to this year's goodest citizen.

268
00:12:34,922 --> 00:12:37,508
-I can't believe I voted for her.
-You voted for her?

269
00:12:37,591 --> 00:12:39,343
[Tarantula]
What? She's good on climate change.

270
00:12:40,594 --> 00:12:44,264
Wait. What's going on?
You've got that twinkle in your eye.

271
00:12:46,350 --> 00:12:49,895
Guys, who's up for another job?

272
00:12:49,978 --> 00:12:51,146
A big one.

273
00:12:52,105 --> 00:12:53,106
[all gasp]

274
00:12:53,857 --> 00:12:55,442
The Golden Dolphin.

275
00:12:55,526 --> 00:12:56,527
Seriously?

276
00:12:56,610 --> 00:12:58,570
Oh! I thought I was
the crazy one.

277
00:12:58,654 --> 00:13:01,156
That job has broken every criminal
who's tried it.

278
00:13:01,240 --> 00:13:03,867
The Bucharest Bandits. Lucky Jim.

279
00:13:03,951 --> 00:13:05,202
The Crimson Paw.

280
00:13:05,285 --> 00:13:07,538
Actually, the Crimson Paw
was never arrested.

281
00:13:07,621 --> 00:13:09,873
Yeah, but he never stole
anything again.

282
00:13:09,957 --> 00:13:13,001
Snake, what better way
to wipe that smirk off

283
00:13:13,085 --> 00:13:14,503
the governor's fuzzy face,

284
00:13:14,586 --> 00:13:17,798
than stealin' the Golden Dolphin
from right under her whiskers?

285
00:13:17,881 --> 00:13:20,509
This is the holy grail of thievery.

286
00:13:20,592 --> 00:13:21,760
If we pull this off,

287
00:13:21,844 --> 00:13:24,888
we'll cement our legacy as
the greatest criminals of all time.

288
00:13:24,972 --> 00:13:26,515
Whoa, whoa, buddy.

289
00:13:26,598 --> 00:13:29,226
I thought we weren't supposed to
make things personal.

290
00:13:29,309 --> 00:13:31,311
Besides, we've got
a good thing goin' here.

291
00:13:31,395 --> 00:13:34,940
Friends, freedom,
and just look at this loot!

292
00:13:36,108 --> 00:13:38,652
All right, you're right. Forget it.
The Dolphin job is off.

293
00:13:38,735 --> 00:13:39,862
Good.

294
00:13:39,945 --> 00:13:42,155
I guess the pig
will get his trophy after all.

295
00:13:42,239 --> 00:13:43,740
Yeah, I guess he would…

296
00:13:45,033 --> 00:13:46,201
What do you mean, "pig"?

297
00:13:46,285 --> 00:13:48,120
Yes, did I not mention that?
That's weird.

298
00:13:48,203 --> 00:13:49,705
I thought I mentioned that it was…

299
00:13:51,081 --> 00:13:52,749
The Good Samaritan is…

300
00:13:52,833 --> 00:13:54,001
A guinea pig?

301
00:13:54,084 --> 00:13:55,836
[shuddering]

302
00:13:55,919 --> 00:13:57,462
What do you say, Snakey?

303
00:13:57,546 --> 00:13:58,797
Better than cake.

304
00:13:58,881 --> 00:14:00,424
[laughing]

305
00:14:00,507 --> 00:14:03,177
[grunts] Okay. Fine.

306
00:14:03,260 --> 00:14:04,928
But he better be delicious.

307
00:14:05,012 --> 00:14:07,514
[laughs] Are we all in this together?

308
00:14:09,016 --> 00:14:10,475
[Wolf] So, here's the plan.

309
00:14:10,976 --> 00:14:15,147
Like every year, the ceremony will be
held at the Museum of Fine Arts,

310
00:14:15,230 --> 00:14:17,482
where the Golden Dolphin
will be positioned

311
00:14:17,566 --> 00:14:19,985
just beyond the backstage curtain.

312
00:14:20,068 --> 00:14:21,153
Sounds easy.

313
00:14:21,236 --> 00:14:22,738
Sounds easy, hermano.

314
00:14:22,821 --> 00:14:25,991
But to get there, we'll need to
bypass three levels of security.

315
00:14:26,074 --> 00:14:27,075
So, step one.

316
00:14:27,993 --> 00:14:29,244
We'll need to blend in.

317
00:14:30,162 --> 00:14:32,789
♪ Baby, I'm howlin' for you ♪

318
00:14:37,294 --> 00:14:38,545
[Wolf] Professor Marmalade,

319
00:14:38,629 --> 00:14:40,881
this year's recipient
of the Golden Dolphin,

320
00:14:40,964 --> 00:14:43,258
the most annoying
good creature on the planet.

321
00:14:43,342 --> 00:14:46,845
Professor, in the past year,
you've stopped wars, fed the hungry

322
00:14:46,929 --> 00:14:48,680
and saved countless pandas.

323
00:14:48,764 --> 00:14:52,601
Some have described your goodness
as second only to Mother Teresa.

324
00:14:52,684 --> 00:14:55,103
Oh, Tiffany.
It's not a competition.

325
00:14:55,187 --> 00:14:57,439
And if it were,
it would really be more of a tie.

326
00:14:57,523 --> 00:14:59,024
But we can all agree

327
00:14:59,107 --> 00:15:01,860
that there is a flower of goodness
inside all of us

328
00:15:01,944 --> 00:15:03,820
just waiting to blossom.

329
00:15:04,905 --> 00:15:06,740
[Wolf] Once inside,
there are two armored doors.

330
00:15:06,823 --> 00:15:09,868
The first can only be opened
by a special key card

331
00:15:09,952 --> 00:15:12,663
that is carried by our dear friend,
the chief of police.

332
00:15:12,746 --> 00:15:15,457
The second is outfitted
with a retinal scanner

333
00:15:15,541 --> 00:15:17,334
and guarded by
an elite special-ops unit

334
00:15:17,417 --> 00:15:20,128
trained to strike first
and ask questions later.

335
00:15:20,212 --> 00:15:21,213
[insect buzzing]

336
00:15:21,922 --> 00:15:24,550
[Wolf]
Governor Foxington is the only one

337
00:15:24,633 --> 00:15:26,718
who has clearance
to open the second door.

338
00:15:26,802 --> 00:15:30,222
So, step two, she and I will need to
get up close and personal.

339
00:15:30,806 --> 00:15:33,016
Enjoy your evening, Mr. Ambassador.

340
00:15:33,100 --> 00:15:34,726
[Wolf] Interesting piece.

341
00:15:34,810 --> 00:15:38,188
Trashy, pointless and pretentious.

342
00:15:38,689 --> 00:15:40,899
Hmm. They say that art reveals

343
00:15:40,983 --> 00:15:42,901
more about the viewer
than the artist.

344
00:15:42,985 --> 00:15:44,069
Mister…

345
00:15:44,152 --> 00:15:47,447
-Poodleton. Oliver Poodleton.
-Okay.

346
00:15:47,531 --> 00:15:52,286
It's about time someone stood up
to those diabolical Bad Guys.

347
00:15:52,369 --> 00:15:55,205
Though, I've got to say,
no one's succeeded yet.

348
00:15:55,289 --> 00:15:57,791
Eh. I don't think it'll be that hard.

349
00:15:57,875 --> 00:16:00,169
I have a feeling
it'll be harder than you think.

350
00:16:00,252 --> 00:16:03,589
I'd say they're one epic job away
from cementing their legacy.

351
00:16:06,717 --> 00:16:08,385
Mr. Poodleton. You're funny.

352
00:16:08,468 --> 00:16:09,678
I am?

353
00:16:09,761 --> 00:16:12,097
The only legacy they're cementing
is life in prison.

354
00:16:12,181 --> 00:16:14,224
Did you see their last job?

355
00:16:14,308 --> 00:16:15,767
Ugh, unsecured exits,

356
00:16:15,851 --> 00:16:18,228
crude disguises,
compulsive showboating.

357
00:16:18,312 --> 00:16:19,646
I mean, it was a mess.

358
00:16:19,730 --> 00:16:22,482
All the classic signs
of a crew in decline.

359
00:16:22,566 --> 00:16:25,485
Next, they're gonna make it personal.

360
00:16:25,569 --> 00:16:27,863
That's when you know they're toast.

361
00:16:28,989 --> 00:16:31,658
Uh, well, that's your opinion.

362
00:16:31,742 --> 00:16:33,785
It is. And I'm the governor.

363
00:16:34,953 --> 00:16:38,582
As for the sculpture,
I think it's about perspective.

364
00:16:39,166 --> 00:16:41,126
If you look closely enough,

365
00:16:41,210 --> 00:16:44,379
even trash can be recycled
into something beautiful.

366
00:16:45,839 --> 00:16:47,925
[Wolf] How about that.

367
00:16:48,759 --> 00:16:51,553
I guess some things
aren't always as they appear.

368
00:16:53,013 --> 00:16:54,431
That reminds me, may I?

369
00:16:54,515 --> 00:16:57,809
I can't miss a photo op with
the governor and a pile of garbage.

370
00:16:57,893 --> 00:17:00,729
Mr. Poodleton,
you're too hard on yourself.

371
00:17:00,812 --> 00:17:01,855
Hey…

372
00:17:03,690 --> 00:17:05,025
[guests chattering]

373
00:17:05,108 --> 00:17:06,401
Okay, friends.

374
00:17:06,484 --> 00:17:08,237
It's showtime.

375
00:17:10,155 --> 00:17:12,324
[Wolf] Once we're in,
it's on to step three.

376
00:17:12,406 --> 00:17:14,367
We split up
and we take our positions.

377
00:17:15,035 --> 00:17:18,704
Officers, if the Bad Guys
crash this event,

378
00:17:18,789 --> 00:17:20,540
I am definitely going to lose my job.

379
00:17:20,624 --> 00:17:24,294
And I will not hesitate to
take you down with me.

380
00:17:24,377 --> 00:17:25,462
Now, move out!

381
00:17:25,546 --> 00:17:26,964
[officers] Yes, ma'am!
Hut, hut, hut, hut!

382
00:17:27,047 --> 00:17:29,341
Hut, hut, hut, hut, hut,
hut, hut, hut, hut, hut!

383
00:17:44,106 --> 00:17:46,358
Mic's on.
Everyone on comms, do you copy?

384
00:17:46,441 --> 00:17:47,442
-Copy.
-Copy.

385
00:17:47,526 --> 00:17:48,902
-Copy.
-Copy.

386
00:17:57,411 --> 00:17:59,121
[Snake laughing]

387
00:18:08,046 --> 00:18:09,464
A drink for the pretty lady?

388
00:18:09,548 --> 00:18:12,843
No, thank you.
My life is too complicated right now.

389
00:18:12,926 --> 00:18:13,927
Uh…

390
00:18:16,346 --> 00:18:18,765
[groans, gags]

391
00:18:41,371 --> 00:18:43,457
Boys, it's dolphin season.

392
00:18:43,540 --> 00:18:44,583
[muffled mumbling]

393
00:18:46,376 --> 00:18:48,045
Copy that. I'm on the move.

394
00:18:50,047 --> 00:18:52,299
Unit Two,
is the backstage area still secure?

395
00:18:52,382 --> 00:18:53,467
[officer] Unit Two. All clear.

396
00:18:53,550 --> 00:18:55,761
This is where
all the training pays off.

397
00:18:55,844 --> 00:18:58,055
-[grunts, groans]
-Pardon me. Terribly sorry.

398
00:18:58,138 --> 00:18:59,681
Not a problem, sir.

399
00:18:59,765 --> 00:19:01,600
Keep your eyes open, boys.

400
00:19:01,683 --> 00:19:04,978
They could be anywhere,
just waiting to humiliate us.

401
00:19:06,146 --> 00:19:07,940
[Wolf laughs]

402
00:19:08,023 --> 00:19:09,566
Wolf is in position.

403
00:19:09,650 --> 00:19:12,277
Piranha,
you all penguin-suited and booted?

404
00:19:12,361 --> 00:19:16,073
Affirmative. I'm a clean, mean
dolphin-stealin' machine.

405
00:19:16,156 --> 00:19:17,491
What's goin' on, guys?

406
00:19:20,953 --> 00:19:22,955
[guests chattering]

407
00:19:53,902 --> 00:19:55,988
-[screams]
-[Wolf grunting]

408
00:19:57,739 --> 00:19:59,992
[old lady panting]

409
00:20:00,075 --> 00:20:02,160
[sighs] Here, let me help you.

410
00:20:03,203 --> 00:20:04,580
Are you okay, ma'am?

411
00:20:04,663 --> 00:20:07,708
[panting] My gracious, yes.

412
00:20:07,791 --> 00:20:11,378
I may be dizzy, but I'm alive!
Thanks to you.

413
00:20:11,461 --> 00:20:12,504
What are you…

414
00:20:12,588 --> 00:20:14,423
Oh. [moans]

415
00:20:14,506 --> 00:20:15,924
[groans]

416
00:20:16,008 --> 00:20:17,926
Thank you, dear.

417
00:20:19,511 --> 00:20:22,055
You're such a good boy.

418
00:20:31,565 --> 00:20:32,566
[grunts]

419
00:20:41,742 --> 00:20:43,160
All good, brother?

420
00:20:43,785 --> 00:20:46,872
Yeah, all good. Yeah, yeah.

421
00:20:46,955 --> 00:20:48,123
Um… [babbling]

422
00:20:48,207 --> 00:20:50,626
Webs, what do you say
about movin' on to step four?

423
00:20:50,709 --> 00:20:53,587
Copy that. Shark, you're up.

424
00:20:53,670 --> 00:20:54,796
Do your thing.

425
00:20:54,880 --> 00:20:56,715
-Do I get to improvise?
-Yes, fine.

426
00:20:56,798 --> 00:20:59,051
Improvise. But please be subtle.

427
00:21:02,721 --> 00:21:05,182
I'm having a baby!

428
00:21:05,265 --> 00:21:06,433
Is there a doctor?

429
00:21:06,517 --> 00:21:08,602
Or perhaps several security guards

430
00:21:08,685 --> 00:21:10,812
that could leave their post
and help me?

431
00:21:10,896 --> 00:21:12,397
-[gasps]
-[elevator bell dings]

432
00:21:12,481 --> 00:21:14,191
[people clamoring]

433
00:21:30,666 --> 00:21:32,084
"Fish surprise"?

434
00:21:33,252 --> 00:21:34,711
Surprise!

435
00:21:34,795 --> 00:21:37,089
-[shouts]
-[security guards grunting]

436
00:21:42,719 --> 00:21:44,346
[Wolf] Hey, Webs,
can you enhance this…

437
00:21:44,429 --> 00:21:46,348
[Tarantula] Done.
Eight steps ahead of you, Wolfie.

438
00:21:53,355 --> 00:21:55,190
-Ah.
-[announcer] Ladies and gentlemen,

439
00:21:55,274 --> 00:21:58,402
your MC for
the Good Samaritan Awards…

440
00:21:58,485 --> 00:21:59,486
[huffing]

441
00:21:59,570 --> 00:22:01,822
[Wolf] All right, Shark, we're in.

442
00:22:01,905 --> 00:22:03,657
Oops, I forgot. I'm not pregnant.

443
00:22:04,283 --> 00:22:06,201
[announcer]
…president of the committee,

444
00:22:06,285 --> 00:22:08,579
Governor Diane Foxington.

445
00:22:08,662 --> 00:22:11,373
Thank you. Thank you.
Thank you so much.

446
00:22:11,456 --> 00:22:12,624
Thank you.

447
00:22:13,959 --> 00:22:16,795
Last year, we faced our biggest test

448
00:22:16,879 --> 00:22:20,549
when a meteorite crashed
into our dear city.

449
00:22:20,632 --> 00:22:23,969
That meteorite didn't just make
a hole in our city,

450
00:22:24,052 --> 00:22:26,013
it made a hole in our hearts.

451
00:22:26,096 --> 00:22:27,097
[guests] Aw.

452
00:22:27,181 --> 00:22:29,975
But even in tragedy,
Professor Marmalade,

453
00:22:30,058 --> 00:22:31,643
he did what he does so well.

454
00:22:31,727 --> 00:22:34,354
He made us
look at things differently.

455
00:22:34,438 --> 00:22:36,064
And thanks to you, Marmalade,

456
00:22:36,148 --> 00:22:39,234
the Love Crater Meteorite
will forever serve

457
00:22:39,318 --> 00:22:41,111
as a symbol of how there is good,

458
00:22:41,195 --> 00:22:43,655
even in the worst places.

459
00:22:43,739 --> 00:22:44,948
[guests applauding]

460
00:22:45,032 --> 00:22:46,450
Whoo!

461
00:22:47,868 --> 00:22:49,578
[Piranha laughs, grunts]

462
00:22:56,502 --> 00:22:57,503
Hurry up.

463
00:22:59,171 --> 00:23:01,798
And successfully reversed
climate change

464
00:23:01,882 --> 00:23:03,967
for the well-being of all of us.

465
00:23:04,051 --> 00:23:06,929
This is going surprisingly smoothly.

466
00:23:15,604 --> 00:23:17,439
What the molt is that?

467
00:23:17,523 --> 00:23:20,609
The Wolf-Piranha-Snake-Shark-
Tarantula Protection System.

468
00:23:20,692 --> 00:23:22,986
-[Tarantula] The W.P.S.S.T.?
-This was not supposed to happen.

469
00:23:23,070 --> 00:23:26,031
-What?
-Guys, calm down. I'm on it.

470
00:23:26,114 --> 00:23:28,283
Initiating
W.P.S.S.T. Override Protocol.

471
00:23:29,493 --> 00:23:30,827
Get it, queen!

472
00:23:32,204 --> 00:23:34,748
-[Wolf] Did it work?
-Just give me five minutes.

473
00:23:34,831 --> 00:23:35,791
[Diane] And now,

474
00:23:35,874 --> 00:23:38,085
please join me in welcoming
to the stage…

475
00:23:38,168 --> 00:23:39,795
We don't have five minutes.

476
00:23:39,878 --> 00:23:41,839
…Professor Marmalade!

477
00:23:41,922 --> 00:23:43,131
-Oh.
-[guests cheering]

478
00:23:43,215 --> 00:23:45,384
We love you,
Professor Marmalade!

479
00:23:45,467 --> 00:23:46,593
The pig is on the move.

480
00:23:46,677 --> 00:23:49,054
I repeat, the pig is on the move.

481
00:23:49,137 --> 00:23:50,138
[Wolf] Webs, Webs!

482
00:23:50,222 --> 00:23:52,766
-The curtain's going up any minute!
-It's not letting me in.

483
00:23:52,850 --> 00:23:54,101
Check your system preferences.

484
00:23:54,184 --> 00:23:55,561
You probably need to
download a driver.

485
00:23:55,644 --> 00:23:56,562
Try rebooting.

486
00:23:56,645 --> 00:23:58,230
Oh, my gosh, you fixed it.

487
00:23:58,313 --> 00:23:59,982
-[Wolf, Snake] Really?
-No!

488
00:24:00,065 --> 00:24:01,108
[Chief] Hey, Larry.

489
00:24:01,817 --> 00:24:04,194
Come on, open up.
What did we say about lockin' doors?

490
00:24:04,278 --> 00:24:06,655
No, no, no.
Shark, I got a situation here.

491
00:24:06,738 --> 00:24:07,990
[Shark] Copy that. I'm on my way.

492
00:24:08,073 --> 00:24:09,825
[stomach gurgling]

493
00:24:09,908 --> 00:24:11,326
Hurry up, guys.

494
00:24:11,410 --> 00:24:13,453
Time to turn this baby on beast mode.

495
00:24:15,998 --> 00:24:17,541
Eat it, W.P.S.S.T.

496
00:24:22,546 --> 00:24:24,423
-[gurgling continues]
-Please, not now.

497
00:24:24,506 --> 00:24:26,175
-[Piranha] Wolf!
-Wait, wait, wait. No, Piranha!

498
00:24:26,258 --> 00:24:27,759
-This award is for…
-[farts]

499
00:24:29,970 --> 00:24:32,014
[clears throat] As I was saying…

500
00:24:32,681 --> 00:24:35,058
No, no, no.

501
00:24:37,769 --> 00:24:39,396
[sniffs]

502
00:24:39,479 --> 00:24:41,273
Piranha! Are you kidding me?

503
00:24:41,356 --> 00:24:42,232
[Piranha] Sorry!

504
00:24:42,316 --> 00:24:44,526
And that's why
my Gala for Goodness

505
00:24:44,610 --> 00:24:47,404
will raise all the money needed
for those less fortunate.

506
00:24:47,487 --> 00:24:48,655
-[Chief] Come on!
-[knocking]

507
00:24:48,739 --> 00:24:49,907
[gasps]

508
00:24:50,657 --> 00:24:52,659
I'm starting to get mad here, Larry.

509
00:24:54,077 --> 00:24:55,162
[Wolf] Webs! Webs!

510
00:24:56,413 --> 00:24:58,999
And now, the moment
we've all been waiting for.

511
00:25:00,584 --> 00:25:01,710
-[Wolf gasps]
-Whoa!

512
00:25:13,180 --> 00:25:15,807
[Shark] Excuse me.
Is this the ladies' room?

513
00:25:16,683 --> 00:25:20,521
Oh, uh, you need to take a right
at the end of the hall, ma'am.

514
00:25:20,604 --> 00:25:22,731
[gasps] Whoa.

515
00:25:25,817 --> 00:25:27,861
Yes! Whoop-bam!

516
00:25:29,321 --> 00:25:30,322
Oh, come on!

517
00:25:30,906 --> 00:25:34,993
And now, it is my honor to award
Professor Marmalade

518
00:25:35,077 --> 00:25:38,914
with the Golden Dolphin!

519
00:25:39,581 --> 00:25:40,707
[guests murmuring]

520
00:25:40,791 --> 00:25:42,251
-No!
-No!

521
00:25:42,334 --> 00:25:45,087
Yes! I mean, yes!

522
00:25:45,879 --> 00:25:47,005
What?

523
00:25:49,758 --> 00:25:50,968
[screams]

524
00:25:52,761 --> 00:25:54,847
Everyone, everyone,
please don't panic.

525
00:25:54,930 --> 00:25:56,515
-[guests murmuring]
-Just stay calm.

526
00:25:56,598 --> 00:25:58,767
I'm sure
there's an explanation for this.

527
00:26:00,102 --> 00:26:03,480
I repeat, please do not panic.

528
00:26:05,524 --> 00:26:07,109
[Wolf] Nice work, everybody.

529
00:26:07,192 --> 00:26:10,404
Now, let's make like a wolf
and get the pack outta here.

530
00:26:10,487 --> 00:26:12,114
Ah, wordplay.

531
00:26:12,781 --> 00:26:13,824
I don't get it.

532
00:26:13,907 --> 00:26:15,534
[Marmalade]
Diane, Diane, if I may…

533
00:26:16,368 --> 00:26:17,661
You have to understand,

534
00:26:17,744 --> 00:26:21,248
I didn't bring hope back to the city
for an award.

535
00:26:21,331 --> 00:26:24,918
I did these good things
because of how they made me feel.

536
00:26:25,002 --> 00:26:28,005
That tingly feeling I get.
That shiver up my spine.

537
00:26:28,088 --> 00:26:31,091
The wag in my tiny tail.

538
00:26:32,551 --> 00:26:33,844
Because you see,

539
00:26:33,927 --> 00:26:38,140
being good just feels so good.

540
00:26:38,223 --> 00:26:41,435
And when you're good, you're loved.

541
00:26:43,729 --> 00:26:45,606
-Huh?
-Wolf?

542
00:26:45,689 --> 00:26:47,024
-What are you doing?
-What are you doing?

543
00:26:47,107 --> 00:26:48,108
-[Tarantula] Go!
-[Shark] Go!

544
00:26:49,234 --> 00:26:50,903
It's the Bad Guys!

545
00:26:50,986 --> 00:26:52,154
Arrest them!

546
00:26:52,237 --> 00:26:54,448
Hut, hut, hut, hut,
hut, hut, hut, hut!

547
00:26:57,868 --> 00:26:59,912
They stole the Golden Dolphin!

548
00:26:59,995 --> 00:27:01,997
Come on, you can't prove that.

549
00:27:02,080 --> 00:27:03,248
[metal clanking]

550
00:27:04,082 --> 00:27:06,043
My baby!

551
00:27:06,126 --> 00:27:08,921
On your knees, Bad Guys,
with your hands up!

552
00:27:09,004 --> 00:27:11,173
Never! We're outta here.

553
00:27:13,717 --> 00:27:15,928
So long, suckers!

554
00:27:22,184 --> 00:27:24,728
Well, this just got a little weird.

555
00:27:24,811 --> 00:27:25,812
[siren wailing]

556
00:27:27,189 --> 00:27:28,899
[Tiffany Fluffit]
The Bad Guys go bust!

557
00:27:28,982 --> 00:27:32,069
The nefarious fivesome
has finally been captured.

558
00:27:32,152 --> 00:27:34,780
And I, Tiffany Fluffit,
am first on the scene.

559
00:27:34,863 --> 00:27:36,865
Wow. You know, I just realized

560
00:27:36,949 --> 00:27:40,118
that I have devoted my entire
adult life to putting you in jail.

561
00:27:40,202 --> 00:27:41,787
You are my purpose.

562
00:27:41,870 --> 00:27:43,872
Without you, who am I?

563
00:27:43,956 --> 00:27:45,040
I'm just kiddin'!

564
00:27:45,123 --> 00:27:47,626
This is the best moment of my life!

565
00:27:47,709 --> 00:27:50,838
It's the end of the Bad Guys.

566
00:27:51,463 --> 00:27:52,339
No!

567
00:27:52,422 --> 00:27:54,424
Get your hands off of me.

568
00:27:54,508 --> 00:27:56,802
You're begging for
a bitin' right now.

569
00:27:56,885 --> 00:27:58,053
Wolf!

570
00:28:02,307 --> 00:28:04,142
[reporter] Professor Marmalade!
Madam Governor!

571
00:28:04,226 --> 00:28:05,310
Professor Marmalade!

572
00:28:05,394 --> 00:28:07,813
-Madam Governor! Madam Governor!
-One at a time. One at a time.

573
00:28:10,357 --> 00:28:11,400
-Hey. Hey!
-Excuse me.

574
00:28:11,483 --> 00:28:13,360
-[reporters gasp]
-Sorry to interrupt,

575
00:28:13,443 --> 00:28:16,154
I just wanted to congratulate
the governor here.

576
00:28:16,238 --> 00:28:18,949
I gotta say,
you really got us pegged.

577
00:28:19,032 --> 00:28:23,287
We're just a deep well
of anger and self-loathing.

578
00:28:23,370 --> 00:28:25,080
-Denial.
-[Wolf] Sure. That too.

579
00:28:25,163 --> 00:28:26,373
-Narcissism.
-[Wolf] Yeah. Yeah.

580
00:28:26,456 --> 00:28:27,708
Emotional emptiness.

581
00:28:27,791 --> 00:28:29,126
So, we're on the same page.

582
00:28:29,209 --> 00:28:31,253
What is he doin'?

583
00:28:31,336 --> 00:28:34,381
Sadly, we were never given a chance

584
00:28:34,464 --> 00:28:37,843
to be anything more
than second-rate criminals.

585
00:28:37,926 --> 00:28:39,970
If only there was someone

586
00:28:40,053 --> 00:28:44,349
who could help the flower of goodness
inside us blossom.

587
00:28:44,433 --> 00:28:47,311
Some icon of love
and forgiveness, like…

588
00:28:48,103 --> 00:28:50,105
I don't know, Mother Teresa.

589
00:28:50,189 --> 00:28:53,108
Best thing is
to just throw us in jail

590
00:28:53,192 --> 00:28:55,152
for the rest of our hopeless lives.

591
00:28:55,235 --> 00:28:57,070
Yeah, that's the plan.

592
00:28:58,071 --> 00:28:59,239
Wait, wait! No, no!

593
00:28:59,323 --> 00:29:01,074
-Get in there.
-Ow!

594
00:29:01,658 --> 00:29:03,744
-[Marmalade] Wait!
-[people murmuring]

595
00:29:03,827 --> 00:29:05,204
B-Beg pardon?

596
00:29:05,287 --> 00:29:07,414
Mr. Wolf may be a savage beast.

597
00:29:07,497 --> 00:29:08,999
Basically, walking garbage.

598
00:29:09,082 --> 00:29:10,417
Sorry, I'm making a point.

599
00:29:10,501 --> 00:29:12,085
Do what you need to do, pal.

600
00:29:12,169 --> 00:29:16,715
But how can we say they're hopeless
if they've never been given a chance?

601
00:29:16,798 --> 00:29:17,841
What if…

602
00:29:17,925 --> 00:29:19,843
What if we tried
a little experiment, Diane?

603
00:29:19,927 --> 00:29:22,221
As you know,
my Gala for Goodness…

604
00:29:22,304 --> 00:29:26,183
the #Charity Event of the Year
is coming up.

605
00:29:26,266 --> 00:29:29,811
If I can prove to everyone at that
gala that the Bad Guys have changed,

606
00:29:29,895 --> 00:29:32,689
will you set them free
and give them a clean start?

607
00:29:32,773 --> 00:29:34,525
[people gasping]

608
00:29:34,608 --> 00:29:36,193
What? Professor Marmalade!

609
00:29:36,276 --> 00:29:37,319
No, no, no.

610
00:29:37,402 --> 00:29:39,780
Don't you see what he's doing?
He's playing you!

611
00:29:39,863 --> 00:29:41,031
But it was my idea.

612
00:29:41,114 --> 00:29:42,241
It was his idea.

613
00:29:42,324 --> 00:29:44,326
But only because
you made him have it!

614
00:29:44,409 --> 00:29:46,787
Madam Governor,
you can't just let them go.

615
00:29:46,870 --> 00:29:49,623
Professor, I'm not about to put
the safety of the city on the line

616
00:29:49,706 --> 00:29:51,166
for an experiment.

617
00:29:51,250 --> 00:29:52,918
Excuse me, Madam Governor.

618
00:29:53,001 --> 00:29:56,505
I seem to remember that
a wise person once said,

619
00:29:56,588 --> 00:30:00,592
"Even trash can be recycled
into something beautiful."

620
00:30:01,468 --> 00:30:02,678
[scoffs]

621
00:30:04,638 --> 00:30:05,931
Okay. I'm game.

622
00:30:06,014 --> 00:30:08,392
But only because it's you, Professor.

623
00:30:08,475 --> 00:30:09,434
No!

624
00:30:09,518 --> 00:30:12,020
We'll hold onto the dolphin
until the gala,

625
00:30:12,104 --> 00:30:15,315
just to remove
any unnecessary temptation.

626
00:30:15,399 --> 00:30:17,526
Of course. Good thinking.

627
00:30:17,609 --> 00:30:19,611
That's why you're governor.

628
00:30:20,445 --> 00:30:21,864
Now that everyone's happy…

629
00:30:21,947 --> 00:30:23,448
Not happy.

630
00:30:23,532 --> 00:30:28,161
…I, Rupert Marmalade the Fourth,
will turn the Bad Guys into

631
00:30:28,245 --> 00:30:29,913
the Good Guys!

632
00:30:29,997 --> 00:30:32,249
[all] Ooh!

633
00:30:34,501 --> 00:30:36,920
I think these belong to you.

634
00:30:37,004 --> 00:30:38,005
Hey!

635
00:30:39,464 --> 00:30:41,508
[Diane] Not everyone
gets a second chance.

636
00:30:42,176 --> 00:30:45,470
Make the most of it, Mr. Poodleton.

637
00:30:51,351 --> 00:30:53,645
[sirens wailing]

638
00:30:55,689 --> 00:30:56,982
[Snake] Wolf.

639
00:30:57,065 --> 00:30:58,317
What are you doing?

640
00:30:58,400 --> 00:30:59,818
-[Wolf] What?
-Yeah.

641
00:30:59,902 --> 00:31:01,320
Oh, that!

642
00:31:02,863 --> 00:31:04,740
I'm sorry, I thought it was obvious.

643
00:31:04,823 --> 00:31:06,742
We're gonna go good.

644
00:31:08,660 --> 00:31:10,037
Uh, you totally lost me.

645
00:31:10,120 --> 00:31:12,164
I told him to stop drinkin'
out of the toilet.

646
00:31:12,247 --> 00:31:14,166
Hey, did you get hit on the head?

647
00:31:14,249 --> 00:31:15,334
What? No, I didn't get…

648
00:31:15,417 --> 00:31:17,294
My cousin got hit on the head
with an anchor,

649
00:31:17,377 --> 00:31:19,213
and after that,
he only swam in a circle.

650
00:31:19,296 --> 00:31:21,215
No, guy, guys, guys.
You're not following me.

651
00:31:21,298 --> 00:31:24,259
We're gonna pretend to go good.

652
00:31:24,343 --> 00:31:26,094
Just a few days with Marmalade.

653
00:31:26,178 --> 00:31:30,098
And then,
we roll into the gala as good guys

654
00:31:30,182 --> 00:31:33,435
and roll out scot-free with…

655
00:31:34,144 --> 00:31:36,355
[all] The Golden Dolphin!

656
00:31:36,438 --> 00:31:37,564
You got it.

657
00:31:37,648 --> 00:31:39,858
Since when do we not finish a job?

658
00:31:39,942 --> 00:31:43,237
The Bad Guys become the Good Guys

659
00:31:43,320 --> 00:31:46,657
so we can stay the bad guys.

660
00:31:46,740 --> 00:31:48,742
-You know what I'm saying?
-[all laughing]

661
00:31:48,825 --> 00:31:50,744
Bad guys acting good?

662
00:31:50,827 --> 00:31:53,664
It's the ultimate bad-guy thing.
It's fantastic.

663
00:31:53,747 --> 00:31:55,374
Wolf, you're a genius!

664
00:31:57,167 --> 00:31:59,503
It's gonna be, like,
the most relaxing con ever.

665
00:31:59,586 --> 00:32:00,921
Like a vacation.

666
00:32:01,004 --> 00:32:03,382
Oh, oh-oh-oh! A con-cation.

667
00:32:03,465 --> 00:32:06,426
-[all laughing]
-[siren wailing continues]

668
00:32:06,510 --> 00:32:08,512
[Shark]
My parents met on a con-cation!

669
00:32:10,472 --> 00:32:12,766
[seagulls squawking]

670
00:32:14,351 --> 00:32:18,105
[Marmalade humming]

671
00:32:21,358 --> 00:32:22,818
[doorbell rings]

672
00:32:22,901 --> 00:32:24,194
Oh, goody!

673
00:32:24,278 --> 00:32:25,612
[Wolf] Wow!

674
00:32:25,696 --> 00:32:27,281
[Tarantula] Big and fancy.

675
00:32:27,364 --> 00:32:30,075
Rodent's got taste. Okay!

676
00:32:30,659 --> 00:32:32,536
Almost makes me wanna be cute.

677
00:32:32,619 --> 00:32:36,039
[Marmalade] They say experience
is the best teacher.

678
00:32:36,123 --> 00:32:38,041
And they are wrong.

679
00:32:38,125 --> 00:32:39,126
I am.

680
00:32:39,209 --> 00:32:41,670
Good morning,
students of goodness.

681
00:32:41,753 --> 00:32:46,758
And welcome to the first day
of the rest of your best life.

682
00:32:46,842 --> 00:32:48,177
A giant butt!

683
00:32:48,760 --> 00:32:49,761
Huh?

684
00:32:49,845 --> 00:32:51,471
Uh, it's-- it's not a butt.

685
00:32:51,555 --> 00:32:55,225
It's a lamp in the shape
of the Love Crater Meteorite,

686
00:32:55,309 --> 00:32:56,268
my greatest…

687
00:32:56,351 --> 00:32:57,436
I wonder whose butt it is.

688
00:32:57,519 --> 00:32:58,770
-[Wolf gasps]
-Uh…

689
00:32:58,854 --> 00:33:01,648
Once again,
it's not a butt, thank you.

690
00:33:01,732 --> 00:33:02,774
It's a heart.

691
00:33:02,858 --> 00:33:04,735
-Now, as I was saying…
-Then why does it have cheeks?

692
00:33:04,818 --> 00:33:05,819
-Shut it!
-What?

693
00:33:05,903 --> 00:33:07,196
I've never seen a heart
with cheeks.

694
00:33:07,279 --> 00:33:09,656
-[chuckles] It's not a…
-Booty!

695
00:33:09,740 --> 00:33:11,742
It's not a butt! Not a butt!

696
00:33:11,825 --> 00:33:13,452
Does he know what a butt is?

697
00:33:14,161 --> 00:33:15,954
[grunts] As I was saying,

698
00:33:16,038 --> 00:33:18,832
on the outside,
the five of you are villains,

699
00:33:18,916 --> 00:33:21,001
predators,
remorseless sociopaths.

700
00:33:21,084 --> 00:33:22,961
Oh, stop,
you're makin' me blush.

701
00:33:23,045 --> 00:33:25,005
But inside, there's a flower.

702
00:33:25,088 --> 00:33:26,798
The flower of goodness.

703
00:33:26,882 --> 00:33:28,175
And when it blooms

704
00:33:28,258 --> 00:33:30,427
and you feel that tingle
of positivity

705
00:33:30,511 --> 00:33:32,262
radiating through your body,

706
00:33:32,346 --> 00:33:35,224
you're going to want to feel it
all the time.

707
00:33:35,307 --> 00:33:36,975
So, we're going for a tingle?

708
00:33:37,059 --> 00:33:38,310
Not any tingle.

709
00:33:38,393 --> 00:33:39,895
The tingle of goodness.

710
00:33:39,978 --> 00:33:44,149
Which you'll feel in my
state-of-the-art Sharing Laboratory!

711
00:33:44,900 --> 00:33:47,945
Okay, Mr. Snake,
I'm going to give you a Push Pop.

712
00:33:48,028 --> 00:33:50,572
Great! Push Pop just for me!

713
00:33:50,656 --> 00:33:52,241
No, to share.

714
00:33:52,324 --> 00:33:53,325
Why?

715
00:33:53,408 --> 00:33:55,452
Well, on a fundamental level,

716
00:33:55,536 --> 00:33:58,705
it's about putting someone else's
needs ahead of your own.

717
00:33:58,789 --> 00:33:59,790
[chuckling]

718
00:33:59,873 --> 00:34:01,500
Oh, no. No way.

719
00:34:01,583 --> 00:34:02,751
Snake…

720
00:34:03,961 --> 00:34:06,171
[sighs] All right, all right.

721
00:34:06,255 --> 00:34:08,382
This is gonna taste extra sweet,

722
00:34:08,465 --> 00:34:10,926
'cause I know how bad you want it.

723
00:34:11,009 --> 00:34:13,469
[groaning]

724
00:34:13,554 --> 00:34:15,931
Pop me, please. Ah!

725
00:34:16,014 --> 00:34:17,474
[groaning]

726
00:34:19,309 --> 00:34:20,601
Nope!

727
00:34:20,686 --> 00:34:23,355
-Sucker!
-That's it! I'll teach you to share!

728
00:34:24,356 --> 00:34:25,357
[all gasp]

729
00:34:25,440 --> 00:34:27,609
I like sharin'. It's yummy. Mmm.

730
00:34:27,693 --> 00:34:29,610
[Snake] Totally worth it.

731
00:34:30,279 --> 00:34:31,780
Well, that's terrifying.

732
00:34:32,281 --> 00:34:33,991
Let's try something simpler.

733
00:34:34,699 --> 00:34:37,953
A good person always pays attention
to the needs of others.

734
00:34:38,036 --> 00:34:40,581
Now, here's a kindly, frail grandma.

735
00:34:41,248 --> 00:34:43,166
[all laughing]

736
00:34:43,250 --> 00:34:46,253
Mr. Piranha,
help Grandma across the street.

737
00:34:46,335 --> 00:34:48,630
Pish! Sure, sure, sure.
I do this all the time.

738
00:34:49,464 --> 00:34:51,091
Here you go, ma'am.

739
00:34:51,175 --> 00:34:52,551
[laughing]

740
00:34:52,634 --> 00:34:54,511
Oh, he is totally gonna blow it.

741
00:34:54,594 --> 00:34:56,847
-What was that? What did you say?
-[Tarantula laughing]

742
00:34:56,929 --> 00:34:58,891
-You think I can't do this?
-No, no, no, Piranha…

743
00:34:58,974 --> 00:34:59,975
[horn honking]

744
00:35:00,058 --> 00:35:02,269
[Wolf screaming, grunts]

745
00:35:03,729 --> 00:35:05,022
Maybe simpler?

746
00:35:05,105 --> 00:35:06,732
[cat meowing]

747
00:35:06,815 --> 00:35:10,110
Hey, look!
It's a cat stuck in a tree.

748
00:35:10,194 --> 00:35:11,987
It doesn't get
much simpler than that.

749
00:35:12,070 --> 00:35:16,116
Now, what in this scenario
would give you that good tingle?

750
00:35:16,200 --> 00:35:19,953
Eating it? This is why I always carry
two pieces of bread with me.

751
00:35:20,037 --> 00:35:23,832
No. I want you to s…

752
00:35:23,916 --> 00:35:25,042
-Smack it.
-Skin it?

753
00:35:25,125 --> 00:35:25,959
Stab it.

754
00:35:26,043 --> 00:35:27,044
-Sauté it.
-Sing to it?

755
00:35:27,127 --> 00:35:29,379
Save it. I want you to save…

756
00:35:29,463 --> 00:35:31,840
It's so obvious…
I want you to save it.

757
00:35:31,924 --> 00:35:34,259
[all] Oh! Right, right.

758
00:35:35,594 --> 00:35:37,763
[all] Here, kitty, kitty cat!

759
00:35:37,846 --> 00:35:38,847
[cat meowing]

760
00:35:38,931 --> 00:35:41,225
Whoa,
that cat is obviously defective.

761
00:35:41,308 --> 00:35:44,311
What is wrong with you?
You're gonna give it a heart attack.

762
00:35:44,394 --> 00:35:45,771
I'll handle this.

763
00:35:46,813 --> 00:35:47,773
What's up, papa!

764
00:35:50,192 --> 00:35:51,193
[yowling]

765
00:35:51,276 --> 00:35:53,195
Get him off my face!
He's on my face!

766
00:35:53,278 --> 00:35:55,322
No, no, no! Listen.
What are you doing?

767
00:35:56,823 --> 00:35:59,284
[Wolf groaning]

768
00:36:00,410 --> 00:36:03,747
Okay. What, may I ask,
are you good at?

769
00:36:04,373 --> 00:36:06,750
-Stealing stuff?
-Oh, yeah, we're great at that.

770
00:36:06,834 --> 00:36:07,876
-Robbery.
-Larceny.

771
00:36:07,960 --> 00:36:09,002
-Wire fraud.
-Extortion.

772
00:36:09,086 --> 00:36:10,254
-Tax evasion.
-Heists.

773
00:36:10,337 --> 00:36:12,381
-[Tarantula] Mail fraud.
-Wait. "Heists," you say?

774
00:36:12,464 --> 00:36:14,716
Well, that's…
Yeah, that's kind of our specialty.

775
00:36:14,800 --> 00:36:17,386
I might just have an idea.

776
00:36:17,719 --> 00:36:20,889
[protestors]
Free the pigs! Free the pigs!

777
00:36:20,973 --> 00:36:22,975
That is an animal testing lab.

778
00:36:23,058 --> 00:36:26,186
Within, 200,000 helpless guinea pigs,

779
00:36:26,270 --> 00:36:30,232
all being poked and prodded
by sadistic scientists.

780
00:36:30,315 --> 00:36:31,692
Guinea pigs, you say?

781
00:36:31,775 --> 00:36:33,110
Snake…

782
00:36:33,193 --> 00:36:34,528
I want you to rescue them.

783
00:36:34,611 --> 00:36:36,780
But this is a heist for good.

784
00:36:36,864 --> 00:36:40,158
So, I brought something
more friendly for you to wear.

785
00:36:40,242 --> 00:36:41,451
Bye.

786
00:36:42,578 --> 00:36:44,288
Well, there goes our street cred.

787
00:36:44,955 --> 00:36:46,164
At least it's comfy.

788
00:36:48,125 --> 00:36:50,752
[Wolf] All right,
we need to distract that scientist.

789
00:36:50,836 --> 00:36:52,963
-Shark, you're up.
-Copy that.

790
00:36:53,046 --> 00:36:55,465
Okay. We're gonna need
a rope and a hook.

791
00:36:55,549 --> 00:36:56,633
I got this one.

792
00:36:56,717 --> 00:36:57,801
-What?
-You're volunteering?

793
00:36:57,885 --> 00:36:59,845
You've never volunteered
for anything.

794
00:36:59,928 --> 00:37:01,930
Sure I did. Right now.

795
00:37:02,014 --> 00:37:04,600
-Throw me up there! Giddy up!
-Really?

796
00:37:04,683 --> 00:37:07,269
Yep.
I'm 99% sure you can make it.

797
00:37:07,352 --> 00:37:09,104
-Okay.
-Let's do it!

798
00:37:10,230 --> 00:37:12,441
-Hey there, son.
-Dad?

799
00:37:12,524 --> 00:37:14,234
I know you've got an important job,

800
00:37:14,318 --> 00:37:16,737
but I hope you still have time
for a catch with your old man.

801
00:37:16,820 --> 00:37:18,530
-[gasps]
-[Snake groans]

802
00:37:18,614 --> 00:37:20,282
-Hey, kiddo.
-[Snake] 96% sure.

803
00:37:20,365 --> 00:37:22,242
You'll always be my special boy.

804
00:37:22,326 --> 00:37:24,912
[groans] Maybe 90%.

805
00:37:24,995 --> 00:37:27,664
I've been waiting my entire life
for this moment.

806
00:37:27,748 --> 00:37:29,750
-Okay, then. Now, go long.
-[Snake] Ow! I don't know.

807
00:37:29,833 --> 00:37:32,503
Oh, boy, oh, boy, oh, boy!
Thank you, Daddy!

808
00:37:32,586 --> 00:37:33,795
[laughing]

809
00:37:34,630 --> 00:37:36,882
Ow! Fifty? What day is it?

810
00:37:36,965 --> 00:37:38,425
[Snake] Who am I?

811
00:37:38,509 --> 00:37:42,262
Right. The guinea pigs are locked
behind a three-foot thick steel door.

812
00:37:42,346 --> 00:37:44,139
The only way in
is through the vents.

813
00:37:44,848 --> 00:37:45,891
I got it.

814
00:37:45,974 --> 00:37:47,267
Upsy-daisy!

815
00:37:47,351 --> 00:37:48,810
♪ Over the filters
And through the vents… ♪

816
00:37:48,894 --> 00:37:51,605
I have never seen him so chipper.
Has he been meditating?

817
00:37:51,688 --> 00:37:54,107
♪ To Guinea Pig Land we… ♪

818
00:37:54,191 --> 00:37:55,359
[Snake screams]

819
00:37:55,442 --> 00:37:57,736
-[squeaking]
-[groans]

820
00:37:57,819 --> 00:37:59,571
[slurping]

821
00:38:00,280 --> 00:38:01,698
Oh.

822
00:38:01,782 --> 00:38:03,909
[whispering] Snake attack.

823
00:38:03,992 --> 00:38:05,369
[protestors chanting]

824
00:38:05,452 --> 00:38:06,954
Hey, look! It's Professor Marmalade.

825
00:38:07,037 --> 00:38:10,791
Yes, that's right.
It's me. Help has arrived.

826
00:38:10,874 --> 00:38:13,210
Just keep your eyes
glued to that door.

827
00:38:13,794 --> 00:38:15,546
Snake. Come on, Snake, open up.

828
00:38:16,171 --> 00:38:19,633
Relax. These doors are complicated.

829
00:38:19,716 --> 00:38:21,718
-[Tarantula] Are you kidding me?
-[guinea pigs squealing]

830
00:38:21,802 --> 00:38:23,136
What do you think you're doing?

831
00:38:23,220 --> 00:38:25,097
We're supposed to save them,
not eat them.

832
00:38:25,180 --> 00:38:27,808
Well, I'd say
they've gone to a better place.

833
00:38:27,891 --> 00:38:28,892
[burps, laughs]

834
00:38:28,976 --> 00:38:30,143
That's it.

835
00:38:30,227 --> 00:38:31,854
Spit them out!

836
00:38:33,647 --> 00:38:35,148
We're gonna save you
whether you like it or not.

837
00:38:35,232 --> 00:38:36,733
We're saving you, stupid hair balls.

838
00:38:36,817 --> 00:38:38,777
Not that door. The other door.

839
00:38:39,945 --> 00:38:40,904
Hey, hey!

840
00:38:41,989 --> 00:38:43,365
Any second.

841
00:38:43,448 --> 00:38:44,449
[yelps]

842
00:38:44,533 --> 00:38:46,660
-[protestors screaming]
-[guinea pigs squealing]

843
00:38:47,369 --> 00:38:48,829
[Marmalade grunts]

844
00:38:49,663 --> 00:38:50,747
[all gasp]

845
00:38:54,251 --> 00:38:55,878
It's not what it looks like.

846
00:38:55,961 --> 00:38:57,796
[alarm blaring]

847
00:39:02,885 --> 00:39:05,304
[Diane] "Trespassing,
burglary, mayhem,

848
00:39:05,387 --> 00:39:08,223
assault with a deadly reptile"?

849
00:39:08,307 --> 00:39:11,185
As if those poor rodents
haven't been through enough already!

850
00:39:11,268 --> 00:39:12,519
No, Diane. Please.

851
00:39:12,603 --> 00:39:17,107
Whoo! Okay. I'm sorry, Professor,
but I'm calling the chief.

852
00:39:17,191 --> 00:39:19,318
-Please. Come on.
-[Diane] This experiment is over.

853
00:39:19,401 --> 00:39:21,737
-[Marmalade] Experiments take time.
-You couldn't help yourself?

854
00:39:21,820 --> 00:39:23,363
So I had a moment of weakness.
Sue me.

855
00:39:23,447 --> 00:39:25,115
That's gonna be difficult
to do from prison!

856
00:39:25,199 --> 00:39:27,284
Guys! What do we do now?

857
00:39:29,244 --> 00:39:32,789
Hmph.
Time to launch a charm offensive.

858
00:39:32,873 --> 00:39:35,918
Oh, yeah. The full Clooney.

859
00:39:37,294 --> 00:39:39,129
Madam Governor. Diane.

860
00:39:39,213 --> 00:39:41,423
Do not Clooney me, Wolf.

861
00:39:41,507 --> 00:39:43,634
I see what's going on.
You think I'm still a bad guy

862
00:39:43,717 --> 00:39:46,053
tryin' to bamboozle my way
to freedom.

863
00:39:46,136 --> 00:39:47,262
But we've changed.

864
00:39:47,346 --> 00:39:49,973
That flower of goodness
is blossoming all over the place.

865
00:39:50,057 --> 00:39:52,768
[sighs]
Don't you ever get tired of lying?

866
00:39:52,851 --> 00:39:54,144
No.

867
00:39:54,228 --> 00:39:55,312
I mean…

868
00:39:55,395 --> 00:39:57,814
Fudge.
That was a trick question, right?

869
00:39:57,898 --> 00:40:00,400
[sighs]
I gave you an opportunity.

870
00:40:00,484 --> 00:40:01,985
A chance to show the world

871
00:40:02,069 --> 00:40:04,279
that you're more
than just a scary stereotype,

872
00:40:04,363 --> 00:40:08,867
but you're too proud or too gutless
to take advantage of it.

873
00:40:08,951 --> 00:40:11,119
Gutless? I'm gutless?

874
00:40:11,203 --> 00:40:13,539
Oh-ho-ho!
I'm sorry, have we met?

875
00:40:13,622 --> 00:40:15,290
I'm the villain of every story.

876
00:40:15,374 --> 00:40:16,792
Guilty until proven innocent.

877
00:40:16,875 --> 00:40:19,545
Even if by some miracle
we did change,

878
00:40:19,628 --> 00:40:21,713
who's gonna believe us, huh?

879
00:40:21,797 --> 00:40:23,507
Of course you wouldn't know
anything about that

880
00:40:23,590 --> 00:40:26,510
with your Little-Miss-Perfect
power suits.

881
00:40:27,928 --> 00:40:29,513
Is that so?

882
00:40:30,722 --> 00:40:33,016
Wait a second, what did…
How did you…

883
00:40:33,100 --> 00:40:36,478
A wolf and a fox
are not so different.

884
00:40:38,146 --> 00:40:40,649
Maybe they will believe you,
maybe they won't.

885
00:40:40,732 --> 00:40:42,025
But it doesn't matter.

886
00:40:42,109 --> 00:40:44,778
Don't do it for them.
Do it for you.

887
00:40:44,862 --> 00:40:47,239
This is a chance
to write your own story,

888
00:40:47,322 --> 00:40:49,825
to find a better life for you
and your friends.

889
00:40:51,034 --> 00:40:52,661
Come on,
what have you got to lose?

890
00:40:52,744 --> 00:40:54,454
I don't know. My dignity?

891
00:40:55,956 --> 00:40:59,209
Yeah, well,
that ship has already sailed.

892
00:40:59,293 --> 00:41:00,752
[car door opens]

893
00:41:05,507 --> 00:41:07,843
Believe it or not,
I'm rootin' for you, Wolf.

894
00:41:09,094 --> 00:41:10,804
So you're not gonna call the chief?

895
00:41:12,055 --> 00:41:13,390
I'll see you at the gala.

896
00:41:32,868 --> 00:41:34,203
[cat meowing]

897
00:41:47,591 --> 00:41:48,634
[meows]

898
00:41:49,468 --> 00:41:52,346
I think we got off
to a bad start.

899
00:41:52,429 --> 00:41:53,889
The name's Wolf.

900
00:41:54,806 --> 00:41:56,183
[shrieks]

901
00:41:56,683 --> 00:41:58,393
Yep. [sighs]

902
00:41:58,477 --> 00:42:01,522
I get that a lot,
first impressions and all.

903
00:42:04,483 --> 00:42:06,401
-[agitated meowing]
-No, no, no!

904
00:42:07,528 --> 00:42:09,279
[yowling]

905
00:42:09,363 --> 00:42:11,365
[panting]

906
00:42:14,451 --> 00:42:16,828
It's okay, it's okay.
I'm not gonna hurt you.

907
00:42:16,912 --> 00:42:19,331
I know you're scared.
I would be, too, if I were you.

908
00:42:21,041 --> 00:42:22,459
Just give me a chance.

909
00:42:23,544 --> 00:42:26,922
Truth is,
we actually have a lot in common.

910
00:42:27,005 --> 00:42:28,215
Don't tell anyone,

911
00:42:28,966 --> 00:42:34,137
but I love a little scratch
on the spot behind my ears.

912
00:42:34,221 --> 00:42:35,639
You know, right there.

913
00:42:36,181 --> 00:42:37,766
The best.

914
00:42:43,146 --> 00:42:44,565
Come on, kitty.

915
00:42:46,066 --> 00:42:47,693
[sniffing]

916
00:42:49,069 --> 00:42:51,238
[purring]

917
00:42:57,744 --> 00:42:59,997
[purring continues]

918
00:43:03,375 --> 00:43:06,044
Yeah. Who's a good kitty?

919
00:43:06,128 --> 00:43:07,713
-Who's a good kitty?
-[Tarantula] Uh, Wolf?

920
00:43:08,338 --> 00:43:10,632
Um, you saved him?

921
00:43:10,716 --> 00:43:11,967
[Marmalade] Yes!

922
00:43:12,718 --> 00:43:15,220
Yes, it's working.

923
00:43:15,304 --> 00:43:16,597
You filmed that?

924
00:43:16,680 --> 00:43:19,683
Yes, and they're starting
to like you.

925
00:43:19,766 --> 00:43:21,643
-Yes!
-All right!

926
00:43:21,727 --> 00:43:24,855
This might just be enough
to win over the guests at the gala.

927
00:43:24,938 --> 00:43:26,857
-Now we're talking!
-All right!

928
00:43:26,940 --> 00:43:29,651
[Tarantula]
Yeah, we did it! All right!

929
00:43:30,402 --> 00:43:31,737
[Marmalade] Uh, Wolf?

930
00:43:31,820 --> 00:43:34,156
I must say,
you've really turned a corner.

931
00:43:34,239 --> 00:43:36,033
-You're really getting it.
-[Wolf] Really?

932
00:43:36,116 --> 00:43:37,826
Oh, thanks.

933
00:43:37,910 --> 00:43:40,787
No, I mean it.
I can see it from tip to tail.

934
00:43:42,372 --> 00:43:44,917
It's just a shame that
you have to carry all that baggage.

935
00:43:46,126 --> 00:43:47,878
What are you talk…
You mean the guys?

936
00:43:48,629 --> 00:43:49,755
[Wolf] What do you mean?

937
00:43:49,838 --> 00:43:51,298
[Marmalade]
You have great potential, Wolf.

938
00:43:51,381 --> 00:43:53,175
But at some point,
you're going to have to choose

939
00:43:53,258 --> 00:43:54,927
between your friends

940
00:43:55,010 --> 00:43:56,178
or the good life.

941
00:44:01,725 --> 00:44:03,769
[Shark, Piranha snoring]

942
00:44:05,395 --> 00:44:07,189
Hey. You still awake?

943
00:44:07,272 --> 00:44:09,233
[cat meowing]

944
00:44:09,316 --> 00:44:10,776
You… You brought the cat in?

945
00:44:10,859 --> 00:44:12,861
Yeah. Yeah.

946
00:44:12,945 --> 00:44:14,905
I'm just savin' it up for later.

947
00:44:14,988 --> 00:44:15,948
Why, what's up?

948
00:44:16,949 --> 00:44:18,867
I was just gettin' a little worried

949
00:44:18,951 --> 00:44:21,328
since you've kinda become a…

950
00:44:21,411 --> 00:44:22,454
Become a what?

951
00:44:22,538 --> 00:44:24,748
You know, teacher's pet.

952
00:44:24,831 --> 00:44:27,251
Gettin' all cozy with Marmalade.

953
00:44:27,334 --> 00:44:29,294
Your tail waggin' and everything.

954
00:44:29,378 --> 00:44:31,797
Well, yeah,
because it has to be believable.

955
00:44:31,880 --> 00:44:34,508
Uh-huh. Yeah, I guess so.

956
00:44:34,591 --> 00:44:36,760
As long as it's all part of the plan.

957
00:44:37,970 --> 00:44:40,347
It is all part of the plan, isn't it?

958
00:44:40,430 --> 00:44:43,851
Snake, buddy,
who made the plan to begin with?

959
00:44:43,934 --> 00:44:44,935
You did.

960
00:44:45,018 --> 00:44:48,564
So I'm the one who sticks to the plan
the most, right?

961
00:44:50,566 --> 00:44:52,109
Yeah, all right. Yeah, okay.

962
00:44:52,192 --> 00:44:54,027
I guess that makes sense, yeah.

963
00:44:54,695 --> 00:44:59,491
But if the plan were ever to change,
you'd tell me, right?

964
00:45:02,286 --> 00:45:03,871
You have my word.

965
00:45:04,454 --> 00:45:05,789
Go bad…

966
00:45:07,207 --> 00:45:08,250
Or go home.

967
00:45:16,925 --> 00:45:18,135
Hey, Snake.

968
00:45:18,218 --> 00:45:19,303
[Snake] Yeah?

969
00:45:19,386 --> 00:45:21,180
You ever wonder what it'd be like?

970
00:45:21,763 --> 00:45:24,558
The world loving us
instead of being scared of us?

971
00:45:24,641 --> 00:45:26,310
You ever… You ever think about that?

972
00:45:26,393 --> 00:45:27,603
[Snake] Loving us?

973
00:45:27,686 --> 00:45:29,479
[laughs] Yeah, right.

974
00:45:29,563 --> 00:45:33,233
I don't waste time thinkin' about
stuff that's never gonna happen.

975
00:45:33,317 --> 00:45:37,196
[sighs] I can't wait for things
to get back to normal.

976
00:45:44,578 --> 00:45:47,164
Yeah. Back to normal, back to normal.

977
00:45:55,923 --> 00:45:58,133
What up!
We are just moments away

978
00:45:58,217 --> 00:46:00,802
from Professor Marmalade's
Gala for Goodness,

979
00:46:00,886 --> 00:46:03,013
where the legendary
Love Crater Meteorite

980
00:46:03,096 --> 00:46:05,599
will be on display
for the first time ever.

981
00:46:05,682 --> 00:46:09,811
But what everyone is really buzzing
about is the Bad Guys

982
00:46:09,895 --> 00:46:11,980
whose heart-melting rescue video

983
00:46:12,064 --> 00:46:15,442
has made them
an overnight viral sensation.

984
00:46:17,361 --> 00:46:19,279
All right, guys, this is the big one.

985
00:46:19,363 --> 00:46:21,740
The Golden Dolphin
is inside a titanium case

986
00:46:21,823 --> 00:46:24,701
controlled by a randomly generated
five-digit code--

987
00:46:24,785 --> 00:46:27,579
a code kept safe and secure
inside a briefcase

988
00:46:27,663 --> 00:46:29,289
handcuffed to the chief of police.

989
00:46:29,373 --> 00:46:31,208
[Piranha] She's not messin' around.

990
00:46:31,291 --> 00:46:34,211
[Wolf] The code is only accessible
with her authorized fingerprints.

991
00:46:34,294 --> 00:46:35,504
[Snake] Leave that to me.

992
00:46:35,587 --> 00:46:38,215
[Wolf] While Snake gets the code,
Shark will secure the fake Dolphin.

993
00:46:38,298 --> 00:46:39,550
[Shark] I like the sound of that.

994
00:46:39,633 --> 00:46:41,635
[Wolf] Meanwhile, the rest of us
plant circuit jammers.

995
00:46:41,718 --> 00:46:44,096
[Tarantula] Allowing me
to hack into the power grid.

996
00:46:44,179 --> 00:46:46,515
[Wolf] At the end of the night,
we toast the professor…

997
00:46:46,598 --> 00:46:47,766
Blah-blah-blah, yada yada…

998
00:46:47,850 --> 00:46:50,435
and when I say "Marmalade,"
the lights go out,

999
00:46:50,519 --> 00:46:52,938
and we'll have exactly four seconds
to make our move.

1000
00:46:53,021 --> 00:46:55,440
[Snake] The old switcheroo.

1001
00:46:55,524 --> 00:46:58,193
[Wolf] Chief hands Marmalade
the fake Dolphin.

1002
00:46:58,277 --> 00:46:59,403
We get our pardon.

1003
00:46:59,486 --> 00:47:01,321
Applause, applause, exit stage right,

1004
00:47:01,405 --> 00:47:03,615
and by the time
they realize what happened…

1005
00:47:03,699 --> 00:47:05,409
So long, suckers!

1006
00:47:05,492 --> 00:47:08,579
