Run!

1144
00:54:11,793 --> 00:54:12,920
Get them!

1145
00:54:20,427 --> 00:54:22,846
Uh…
[nervous chuckle]

1146
00:54:26,892 --> 00:54:28,185
Here, here.

1147
00:54:28,268 --> 00:54:30,103
-What are you doing?
-I'm giving it all back.

1148
00:54:30,771 --> 00:54:31,813
Huh?

1149
00:54:33,649 --> 00:54:34,858
[Wolf] Excuse me.

1150
00:54:38,195 --> 00:54:39,404
What happened back there?

1151
00:54:39,488 --> 00:54:41,740
-I couldn't do it.
-What do you mean you couldn't do it?

1152
00:54:41,823 --> 00:54:43,116
-[Wolf] I just…
-No!

1153
00:54:43,200 --> 00:54:45,035
I do not run.

1154
00:54:45,118 --> 00:54:47,454
That is not how I roll.

1155
00:54:47,538 --> 00:54:49,248
Piranha, don't do anything crazy.

1156
00:54:49,331 --> 00:54:50,874
Ha-ha-ha-ha!

1157
00:54:50,958 --> 00:54:54,002
"Crazy" is what I bring
to the party, chico.

1158
00:54:58,841 --> 00:55:00,509
[Shark groans]

1159
00:55:02,261 --> 00:55:04,513
You're makin' a mistake.
We didn't do it.

1160
00:55:04,596 --> 00:55:06,974
I know we always say that,
but this time it's actually true.

1161
00:55:07,057 --> 00:55:08,976
La, la, la, la, la. Can't hear you.

1162
00:55:09,059 --> 00:55:11,353
-Guilty, guilty, guilty!
-Talk to Marmalade.

1163
00:55:11,436 --> 00:55:13,230
We're really good now.
He'll tell you.

1164
00:55:13,313 --> 00:55:14,481
Professor…

1165
00:55:14,565 --> 00:55:16,859
Tonight's headline:
Change is Impossible.

1166
00:55:16,942 --> 00:55:18,944
You should always judge a book
by its cover,

1167
00:55:19,027 --> 00:55:21,405
and all stereotypes
have been affirmed.

1168
00:55:21,488 --> 00:55:24,324
Stop, for goodness' sake!
Let me speak to them.

1169
00:55:24,408 --> 00:55:26,702
I'm sure there's been
some misunderstanding.

1170
00:55:27,411 --> 00:55:28,412
[door opens]

1171
00:55:28,495 --> 00:55:30,038
[sighs] Professor Marmalade.

1172
00:55:30,122 --> 00:55:33,584
You've got five minutes.
No deals this time.

1173
00:55:33,667 --> 00:55:36,628
You have to help us. Tell them.
Tell them we didn't do it.

1174
00:55:36,712 --> 00:55:39,590
There, there. Of course
you didn't do it. How could you?

1175
00:55:39,673 --> 00:55:43,177
After all, you're such a good boy.

1176
00:55:44,428 --> 00:55:47,181
You're such a good boy.

1177
00:55:47,264 --> 00:55:51,894
That shiver up my spine.
The wag in my tiny tail.

1178
00:55:51,977 --> 00:55:52,811
Arrest them!

1179
00:55:52,895 --> 00:55:54,897
What if we tried
a little experiment, Diane?

1180
00:55:54,980 --> 00:55:57,441
As you know,
my Gala for Goodness…

1181
00:55:57,524 --> 00:55:59,693
[Tiffany Fluffit] Where the legendary
Love Crater Meteorite

1182
00:55:59,776 --> 00:56:02,487
will be on display
for the first time ever.

1183
00:56:02,571 --> 00:56:05,490
All eyes will be on you tonight,
not me.

1184
00:56:06,617 --> 00:56:07,659
You're such a…

1185
00:56:07,743 --> 00:56:09,995
[low voice] Good boy.

1186
00:56:10,913 --> 00:56:12,623
You.

1187
00:56:12,706 --> 00:56:14,541
It was all you.

1188
00:56:14,625 --> 00:56:15,959
What are you talkin' about, Wolf?

1189
00:56:16,043 --> 00:56:18,212
The old lady, the Golden Dolphin,
good training…

1190
00:56:18,295 --> 00:56:19,588
It was all to get us here

1191
00:56:19,671 --> 00:56:22,007
so he could steal the meteorite
and let us take the fall.

1192
00:56:22,090 --> 00:56:23,759
Whoa, what old lady?

1193
00:56:23,842 --> 00:56:26,595
And why would a guinea pig
want a meteorite anyway?

1194
00:56:26,678 --> 00:56:28,931
[Marmalade cackling]

1195
00:56:29,014 --> 00:56:31,767
Uh, guys? He's creepin' me out.

1196
00:56:31,850 --> 00:56:32,935
Wait, what?

1197
00:56:33,018 --> 00:56:35,020
What's goin' on?
Someone turn me around.

1198
00:56:35,103 --> 00:56:38,774
Well, well. So, you finally get it.

1199
00:56:38,857 --> 00:56:40,025
[all] What?

1200
00:56:40,108 --> 00:56:41,944
You stole the meteorite?

1201
00:56:42,027 --> 00:56:44,071
It's not just a meteorite.

1202
00:56:44,154 --> 00:56:45,531
I told you guys it's a butt.

1203
00:56:45,614 --> 00:56:46,865
It's not a butt!

1204
00:56:47,533 --> 00:56:51,036
[exhales]
It's the ultimate power source.

1205
00:56:51,119 --> 00:56:52,871
You see, when it struck,

1206
00:56:52,955 --> 00:56:55,707
scientists found that it emitted
an electromagnetic frequency

1207
00:56:55,791 --> 00:56:57,876
unlike anything else on earth.

1208
00:56:57,960 --> 00:56:59,753
I'm going to harness its power

1209
00:56:59,837 --> 00:57:02,798
to pull off the greatest heist
the world has ever seen.

1210
00:57:03,882 --> 00:57:05,676
You should've eaten him
when you had the chance.

1211
00:57:05,759 --> 00:57:07,386
-Yep.
-But why us?

1212
00:57:07,469 --> 00:57:09,930
Because you're the perfect patsies.

1213
00:57:10,013 --> 00:57:13,267
Come on, when people look up "bad"
in the dictionary,

1214
00:57:13,350 --> 00:57:15,936
do they see a sweet,
adorable guinea pig?

1215
00:57:16,019 --> 00:57:17,855
No. They see you.

1216
00:57:18,564 --> 00:57:19,982
And they always will.

1217
00:57:20,065 --> 00:57:21,483
Okay. Fine.

1218
00:57:21,567 --> 00:57:23,068
But you set us up.

1219
00:57:23,151 --> 00:57:24,653
Oh, pish-pish.

1220
00:57:24,736 --> 00:57:28,115
Let's be honest.
Evolution set you up.

1221
00:57:28,198 --> 00:57:30,284
But Wolfie here really clinched it.

1222
00:57:30,367 --> 00:57:32,870
You fell for every one of my traps,

1223
00:57:32,953 --> 00:57:36,039
starting with saving
a helpless little old lady.

1224
00:57:36,540 --> 00:57:39,501
Wolf. What's he talkin' about?

1225
00:57:42,379 --> 00:57:43,672
[Marmalade] Whoops.

1226
00:57:43,755 --> 00:57:45,716
Did I say too much?

1227
00:57:46,800 --> 00:57:49,136
Anyhoo, looks like yet again

1228
00:57:49,219 --> 00:57:52,806
the big, bad wolf got outsmarted
by a little piggy.

1229
00:57:52,890 --> 00:57:55,767
[growls]
You little pouchy-cheeked rat!

1230
00:57:55,851 --> 00:57:57,436
I'll kill you, you hear me?

1231
00:57:57,519 --> 00:57:59,354
-[Marmalade] Help! Help!
-You're dead! You're dead…

1232
00:57:59,438 --> 00:58:01,815
Help!
The big, bad wolf is attacking me.

1233
00:58:01,899 --> 00:58:04,234
Now you are done forever, Wolf!

1234
00:58:09,781 --> 00:58:13,160
[sirens wailing]

1235
00:58:13,243 --> 00:58:14,286
[Marmalade shuddering]

1236
00:58:14,369 --> 00:58:17,247
Professor, Professor,
any thoughts on how the Bad Guys

1237
00:58:17,331 --> 00:58:19,666
managed to steal the meteorite
in plain sight?

1238
00:58:19,750 --> 00:58:21,251
Well, off the top of my head,

1239
00:58:21,335 --> 00:58:22,961
perhaps they accessed
the site previously

1240
00:58:23,045 --> 00:58:25,506
and set up an intricate system
of tunnels and trapdoors

1241
00:58:25,589 --> 00:58:26,924
that could be remotely triggered

1242
00:58:27,007 --> 00:58:28,884
to suck the meteorite
down into a holding area.

1243
00:58:28,967 --> 00:58:30,511
-But how should I know?
-[Tiffany Fluffit] Totally.

1244
00:58:30,594 --> 00:58:33,597
[Marmalade] I mean, they're
the deranged masterminds. Not me.

1245
00:58:55,702 --> 00:58:57,079
[Wolf] I'm giving it all back.

1246
00:59:22,396 --> 00:59:25,232
I can't believe we got double-crossed
by a tiny rodent.

1247
00:59:25,315 --> 00:59:27,901
Oh, we got double-crossed
by a rodent, all right.

1248
00:59:27,985 --> 00:59:29,903
But, uh, not a tiny one.

1249
00:59:29,987 --> 00:59:31,071
What?

1250
00:59:31,154 --> 00:59:33,991
This was supposed to be
us conning Marmalade.

1251
00:59:34,074 --> 00:59:36,994
It turns out, it was Wolf conning us.

1252
00:59:37,077 --> 00:59:38,829
[gagging]

1253
00:59:38,912 --> 00:59:40,747
Does that sound familiar
to you, Wolf?

1254
00:59:40,831 --> 00:59:42,124
Why would you think that?

1255
00:59:42,207 --> 00:59:44,877
I don't know,
maybe because you just sabotaged

1256
00:59:44,960 --> 00:59:47,087
the biggest heist of our lives?

1257
00:59:47,171 --> 00:59:49,464
I think you owe us
an explanation, buddy.

1258
00:59:50,716 --> 00:59:51,717
[sighs]

1259
00:59:51,800 --> 00:59:53,343
Okay. You're right.

1260
00:59:53,427 --> 00:59:54,511
This is what happened.

1261
00:59:54,595 --> 00:59:58,015
Back in the museum, I just tried
to steal an old lady's purse.

1262
00:59:58,098 --> 00:59:59,349
Classic snatch and grab.

1263
00:59:59,433 --> 01:00:00,976
"Tried to"?

1264
01:00:01,059 --> 01:00:03,770
Since when do you try to steal
something and not just steal it?

1265
01:00:03,854 --> 01:00:07,232
I was trying to steal the purse,
when the old lady fell…

1266
01:00:07,316 --> 01:00:09,109
[clears throat]
…and I kinda helped her.

1267
01:00:09,193 --> 01:00:10,152
What?

1268
01:00:10,235 --> 01:00:12,279
I kinda helped her.

1269
01:00:12,362 --> 01:00:13,572
But then you stole her purse?

1270
01:00:13,655 --> 01:00:15,407
No. I didn't.

1271
01:00:15,490 --> 01:00:17,201
I saved the old lady,

1272
01:00:17,284 --> 01:00:19,703
and she hugged me,
and my tail wagged,

1273
01:00:19,786 --> 01:00:22,748
and I didn't know what it was,
but it felt, you know…

1274
01:00:23,373 --> 01:00:24,374
good.

1275
01:00:24,458 --> 01:00:25,959
[all gasp]

1276
01:00:26,043 --> 01:00:28,921
Ah! But then,
you stole the purse?

1277
01:00:29,004 --> 01:00:30,631
[all] No!

1278
01:00:30,714 --> 01:00:34,384
You know, I heard what the pig said
to you about cuttin' us loose.

1279
01:00:34,468 --> 01:00:36,720
Wait. Like, "us" us?

1280
01:00:36,803 --> 01:00:39,014
But I never thought
you'd actually do it, man.

1281
01:00:39,097 --> 01:00:40,224
Hey, hey, hey, hey.

1282
01:00:40,307 --> 01:00:42,768
I would never… I was tryin' to…

1283
01:00:42,851 --> 01:00:44,853
I was trying to find us
a better life.

1284
01:00:44,937 --> 01:00:48,649
Our life was perfect
until you decided to ruin it.

1285
01:00:48,732 --> 01:00:49,733
[Wolf] I didn't.

1286
01:00:49,816 --> 01:00:52,027
You guys felt it at the gala.

1287
01:00:52,110 --> 01:00:54,071
The clapping, the cheering.

1288
01:00:54,154 --> 01:00:56,949
We were more than
just scary villains. They loved us.

1289
01:00:57,032 --> 01:00:59,618
Oh, yeah? If they loved us so much,

1290
01:00:59,701 --> 01:01:02,704
how come we're in prison
for a crime we didn't commit?

1291
01:01:03,330 --> 01:01:04,289
You know what?

1292
01:01:04,373 --> 01:01:05,832
I'll give Marmalade this:

1293
01:01:05,916 --> 01:01:07,960
At least he sees the world
for what it is:

1294
01:01:08,043 --> 01:01:12,005
A place where some people are scary
and some people are scared.

1295
01:01:12,089 --> 01:01:15,509
Oh, yeah?
Well, I'm tired of bein' scary.

1296
01:01:15,592 --> 01:01:17,511
I'm tired of bein' an outcast.

1297
01:01:17,594 --> 01:01:19,972
-Maybe I don't wanna be a--
-What? A bad guy?

1298
01:01:20,055 --> 01:01:22,391
Don't wanna be
a bad guy anymore, huh?

1299
01:01:22,474 --> 01:01:23,642
Say it, Wolf!

1300
01:01:26,270 --> 01:01:27,813
Yeah, I thought so.

1301
01:01:27,896 --> 01:01:30,357
And us? Your lifelong friends?

1302
01:01:30,440 --> 01:01:31,567
We're just holdin' you back?

1303
01:01:31,650 --> 01:01:33,318
Yeah, maybe you are!

1304
01:01:34,444 --> 01:01:35,779
[gasps]

1305
01:01:37,281 --> 01:01:38,448
-Take it back.
-Snake!

1306
01:01:38,532 --> 01:01:40,200
Take it back! Apologize!

1307
01:01:40,284 --> 01:01:42,160
Hey, hey, hey!

1308
01:01:42,244 --> 01:01:43,996
Prison is no place for fighting.

1309
01:01:45,414 --> 01:01:46,748
Tell that to him.

1310
01:01:46,832 --> 01:01:47,833
[Wolf] Huh?

1311
01:01:52,754 --> 01:01:54,882
-What?
-[shouting]

1312
01:02:01,263 --> 01:02:03,265
[grunts, shouts]

1313
01:02:03,348 --> 01:02:04,349
[shouts]

1314
01:02:07,519 --> 01:02:09,438
[high-pitched shout, screams]

1315
01:02:11,190 --> 01:02:12,524
-[guard screaming]
-Shh.

1316
01:02:19,156 --> 01:02:20,490
[shouts]

1317
01:02:24,912 --> 01:02:26,705
[screams]

1318
01:02:34,546 --> 01:02:36,548
[both grunt]

1319
01:02:38,008 --> 01:02:39,384
Wait, wait! Hold…

1320
01:02:41,094 --> 01:02:42,888
[all gasp] Diane?

1321
01:02:42,971 --> 01:02:45,390
But how do you know how to do
all of that kick-kick-punch-punch?

1322
01:02:45,474 --> 01:02:47,893
Wait a sec, you're the Crimson Paw?

1323
01:02:50,521 --> 01:02:53,190
[Wolf] The Queen of Cons,
Acrobatic Swiss Army Knife,

1324
01:02:53,273 --> 01:02:55,776
stole the Zumpango diamond twice,
once for profit,

1325
01:02:55,859 --> 01:02:57,402
second time just for fun.

1326
01:02:57,486 --> 01:03:00,113
Never identified, never caught.

1327
01:03:00,197 --> 01:03:04,243
[chuckles] Guess I'm still the best
bad guy the world has ever seen.

1328
01:03:05,118 --> 01:03:07,454
-[sighs] At least I used to be.
-[alarm blaring]

1329
01:03:07,538 --> 01:03:09,414
-[guards screaming]
-[Wolf, Shark gasp]

1330
01:03:13,252 --> 01:03:14,336
[screams]

1331
01:03:17,923 --> 01:03:19,842
Nope, I am still the best.

1332
01:03:19,925 --> 01:03:22,302
Just like riding a stolen bicycle.

1333
01:03:22,886 --> 01:03:25,013
Oh. Uh, you got a little… Ouch.

1334
01:03:25,097 --> 01:03:27,349
Hey, why…
Why did you save us anyway?

1335
01:03:27,432 --> 01:03:29,726
After the gala,
I knew something wasn't right.

1336
01:03:29,810 --> 01:03:31,728
So, I did some investigating,
and that meteor…

1337
01:03:31,812 --> 01:03:32,813
I know.

1338
01:03:32,896 --> 01:03:35,566
Some kinda
cosmic-mega-super-antennae thing.

1339
01:03:35,649 --> 01:03:38,193
Right. If conducted through
an array of ionized crystals,

1340
01:03:38,277 --> 01:03:40,279
it will generate
a massive psychokinetic field

1341
01:03:40,362 --> 01:03:41,655
the size of a city.

1342
01:03:41,738 --> 01:03:44,324
Oh, my gosh, did I interrupt you?
Were you gonna say that?

1343
01:03:44,408 --> 01:03:46,910
Uh… I was gonna be
a little more technical,

1344
01:03:46,994 --> 01:03:49,413
-but you got the gist of it.
-[Diane laughs]

1345
01:03:50,914 --> 01:03:54,168
Marmalade needs to be stopped,
but I can't do it alone.

1346
01:03:54,251 --> 01:03:56,128
You know his compound
better than anyone.

1347
01:03:56,211 --> 01:03:57,838
You can count on us.

1348
01:03:57,921 --> 01:03:59,214
Right, guys?

1349
01:04:00,048 --> 01:04:01,550
There is no "us."

1350
01:04:01,633 --> 01:04:03,177
We're through, Wolf.

1351
01:04:03,260 --> 01:04:05,095
Done. Finito.

1352
01:04:05,179 --> 01:04:06,889
Because of
that little tiff back there?

1353
01:04:06,972 --> 01:04:09,725
Come on, man, that's what we do.

1354
01:04:09,808 --> 01:04:11,894
You serve, I volley.
That's our little dance.

1355
01:04:13,187 --> 01:04:14,521
Not this time.

1356
01:04:20,068 --> 01:04:21,069
Piranha?

1357
01:04:24,990 --> 01:04:26,033
Webs?

1358
01:04:26,116 --> 01:04:27,409
Sorry, Wolfie.

1359
01:04:29,536 --> 01:04:30,704
Shark…

1360
01:04:30,787 --> 01:04:32,247
Hmm.

1361
01:04:32,331 --> 01:04:33,498
Hey.

1362
01:04:34,416 --> 01:04:35,417
Guys?

1363
01:04:36,585 --> 01:04:37,878
Guys?

1364
01:04:39,046 --> 01:04:41,173
You wanna know
why I hate birthdays, Wolf?

1365
01:04:41,256 --> 01:04:42,132
Do you?

1366
01:04:43,884 --> 01:04:47,721
When you grow up a snake,
nobody shows up to your party.

1367
01:04:47,804 --> 01:04:50,849
Birthdays are a constant reminder
that out there

1368
01:04:50,933 --> 01:04:55,479
I'm just a scary,
good-for-nothin' monster.

1369
01:04:57,105 --> 01:04:58,148
Yeah.

1370
01:04:59,107 --> 01:05:01,860
But nothing compares
to havin' the one guy--

1371
01:05:01,944 --> 01:05:05,239
the one guy I thought I could trust--

1372
01:05:05,781 --> 01:05:07,074
stab me in the back.

1373
01:05:11,203 --> 01:05:13,288
Come on, guys. Let's get outta here.

1374
01:05:42,192 --> 01:05:43,944
[helicopter approaching]

1375
01:05:54,246 --> 01:05:56,248
[electricity crackling]

1376
01:06:00,836 --> 01:06:04,673
Now, this is what a true bad guy
looks like.

1377
01:06:04,756 --> 01:06:06,633
[helmet whirs]

1378
01:06:11,471 --> 01:06:13,265
What do you say we have some fun?

1379
01:06:18,645 --> 01:06:19,688
[maniacal laughing]

1380
01:06:21,440 --> 01:06:23,192
[laughing continues]

1381
01:06:25,652 --> 01:06:27,779
[screeching]

1382
01:06:39,082 --> 01:06:40,292
[gasping]

1383
01:06:42,586 --> 01:06:44,838
[people screaming]

1384
01:06:52,387 --> 01:06:53,388
Hey.

1385
01:06:54,223 --> 01:06:55,224
You okay?

1386
01:06:55,891 --> 01:06:57,100
No, I'm not okay.

1387
01:06:57,184 --> 01:06:59,436
I'm very, very un-okay.

1388
01:07:00,312 --> 01:07:03,857
Um, I just left the only friends
I have ever had, so what am…

1389
01:07:04,900 --> 01:07:06,109
What am I doin'?

1390
01:07:07,486 --> 01:07:08,612
[sighs]

1391
01:07:09,154 --> 01:07:10,906
I know this isn't easy,

1392
01:07:11,990 --> 01:07:13,367
leaving everything behind.

1393
01:07:14,284 --> 01:07:16,036
-Do you?
-Yeah.

1394
01:07:16,119 --> 01:07:18,288
I was the best thief in the world.

1395
01:07:18,372 --> 01:07:21,416
Fast, fearless, inventive.

1396
01:07:22,501 --> 01:07:24,753
I just had one thing left to steal.

1397
01:07:25,337 --> 01:07:26,839
The Golden Dolphin.

1398
01:07:26,922 --> 01:07:27,965
So you went after it.

1399
01:07:29,049 --> 01:07:30,467
I didn't just go after it.

1400
01:07:32,135 --> 01:07:33,554
I had it.

1401
01:07:33,637 --> 01:07:35,597
And a clear escape route.

1402
01:07:38,851 --> 01:07:39,852
But…

1403
01:07:41,186 --> 01:07:43,689
all I saw in the end
was the tricky fox

1404
01:07:43,772 --> 01:07:45,607
that they always told me I was.

1405
01:07:47,609 --> 01:07:49,027
It changed everything.

1406
01:07:50,153 --> 01:07:53,907
So, now, instead of hurting people,
I'm helping them.

1407
01:07:53,991 --> 01:07:55,701
I'm still me. [chuckles]

1408
01:07:55,784 --> 01:07:58,871
I'm just me, on the right side.

1409
01:08:00,706 --> 01:08:02,708
You're doing the right thing.

1410
01:08:02,791 --> 01:08:05,460
And some day, your friends,
if they're real friends,

1411
01:08:06,170 --> 01:08:07,671
I think they'll understand.

1412
01:08:09,047 --> 01:08:10,966
Now, come on, let's get inside.

1413
01:08:11,049 --> 01:08:12,843
You look like
you just busted out of a prison.

1414
01:08:12,926 --> 01:08:13,927
[chuckling]

1415
01:08:14,011 --> 01:08:15,179
-[thuds]
-[both gasp]

1416
01:08:15,262 --> 01:08:17,014
[guinea pig chittering]

1417
01:08:17,096 --> 01:08:18,390
Guinea pigs?

1418
01:08:18,473 --> 01:08:20,267
-[gasps]
-[both] Marmalade!

1419
01:08:20,350 --> 01:08:21,268
Let's bounce.

1420
01:08:23,395 --> 01:08:25,856
So, this is the hideout
of the great Crimson Paw.

1421
01:08:25,939 --> 01:08:27,191
-[Diane chuckles]
-[keypad beeping]

1422
01:08:27,274 --> 01:08:28,442
Snack break?

1423
01:08:28,524 --> 01:08:31,028
Okay, oddly timed, but you do you.

1424
01:08:31,111 --> 01:08:33,029
-[automated voice] Identity verified.
-What?

1425
01:08:33,113 --> 01:08:34,573
Welcome, Diane.

1426
01:08:40,370 --> 01:08:41,580
Whoa!

1427
01:08:41,662 --> 01:08:44,124
Holy moly!

1428
01:08:44,207 --> 01:08:46,335
Ah! It's so good to be home.

1429
01:08:46,417 --> 01:08:47,627
Are you kiddin' me?

1430
01:08:47,711 --> 01:08:49,212
Laser-sighted zip line?

1431
01:08:49,296 --> 01:08:52,216
The XM 2400 Radar Jammer? No way!

1432
01:08:52,299 --> 01:08:54,301
I actually prefer the earlier model.

1433
01:08:54,384 --> 01:08:56,511
Agree to disagree.

1434
01:08:56,595 --> 01:08:59,055
This stuff is nice too. [screams]

1435
01:08:59,139 --> 01:09:00,724
Yeah, that's a blowtorch.

1436
01:09:00,807 --> 01:09:02,559
Also, not really your color.

1437
01:09:02,643 --> 01:09:03,685
Ugh.

1438
01:09:03,769 --> 01:09:04,937
[Diane] All righty.

1439
01:09:05,020 --> 01:09:09,649
Marmalade, what are you up to,
you fuzzy little weirdo?

1440
01:09:09,733 --> 01:09:11,151
We need eyes on the city.

1441
01:09:11,234 --> 01:09:14,613
Let's see if we can't hack into the
government's surveillance satellite.

1442
01:09:14,696 --> 01:09:16,365
But you're the governor.
Couldn't you just ask?

1443
01:09:16,448 --> 01:09:17,991
Yeah, but the paperwork.

1444
01:09:18,075 --> 01:09:19,618
[beeping]

1445
01:09:19,701 --> 01:09:23,205
[Diane mumbling]

1446
01:09:23,287 --> 01:09:27,125
I am definitely picking up on
suspicious activity here.

1447
01:09:27,209 --> 01:09:29,336
Those are guinea pig heat signatures.

1448
01:09:29,419 --> 01:09:31,587
Marmalade seems to be
controlling them.

1449
01:09:32,256 --> 01:09:33,756
But to do what?

1450
01:09:33,841 --> 01:09:35,050
There are no obvious targets.

1451
01:09:38,011 --> 01:09:39,720
That's because
they're moving targets.

1452
01:09:39,805 --> 01:09:42,349
[gasps] His charity fundraiser.

1453
01:09:42,432 --> 01:09:45,352
He's gonna steal the money.
Raised in his own name?

1454
01:09:45,435 --> 01:09:47,895
It's the greatest heist
the world's ever seen.

1455
01:09:47,979 --> 01:09:50,232
One billion dollars inside trucks

1456
01:09:50,314 --> 01:09:52,317
on their way to charities
all over the city.

1457
01:09:52,401 --> 01:09:53,861
We need to cut off
Marmalade's communication

1458
01:09:53,944 --> 01:09:54,945
with his guinea pig army.

1459
01:09:55,028 --> 01:09:56,530
If there's no signal…

1460
01:09:56,613 --> 01:09:57,865
There's no heist.

1461
01:09:57,948 --> 01:10:00,450
[both]
We have to steal the meteorite.

1462
01:10:00,534 --> 01:10:01,577
That was very cute…

1463
01:10:01,660 --> 01:10:02,953
-All right.
-…what we just did there.

1464
01:10:03,036 --> 01:10:05,372
Put on your big-girl pants.
We're gearin' up.

1465
01:10:11,879 --> 01:10:14,298
I wouldn't take that. Those things
rip your pants right off.

1466
01:10:14,381 --> 01:10:17,718
Huh. Try wearing clean underwear.
Just in case.

1467
01:10:18,927 --> 01:10:20,012
What…

1468
01:10:21,805 --> 01:10:23,682
You stole my car?

1469
01:10:23,765 --> 01:10:25,434
Respect.

1470
01:10:26,018 --> 01:10:27,728
Let's do this.

1471
01:10:37,404 --> 01:10:39,239
-[elevator bell dings]
-[all gasp]

1472
01:10:39,323 --> 01:10:40,365
-[Shark] No!
-[Snake] What?

1473
01:10:40,449 --> 01:10:41,658
[Piranha] All our stuff?

1474
01:10:42,284 --> 01:10:43,911
-[Tarantula] Oh, no.
-Where is everything?

1475
01:10:43,994 --> 01:10:46,205
-No, no, no!
-All our stuff.

1476
01:10:46,288 --> 01:10:48,415
-It's all gone!
-My disguise closet!

1477
01:10:48,498 --> 01:10:49,958
[Tarantula]
Where's my things?

1478
01:10:51,335 --> 01:10:53,754
Wolf gave away all our loot!

1479
01:10:53,837 --> 01:10:56,298
We stole it fair and square!

1480
01:10:56,381 --> 01:10:59,801
Now I understand what it feels like
to have things stolen from you.

1481
01:11:00,344 --> 01:11:02,346
[panting] I don't like it.

1482
01:11:03,055 --> 01:11:06,308
I really don't like it! [whimpering]

1483
01:11:09,394 --> 01:11:12,773
-[grumbles]
-[Shark crying] We got no food.

1484
01:11:12,856 --> 01:11:15,067
We got no money. We got no money
we could use to buy food.

1485
01:11:15,150 --> 01:11:16,652
No food we can sell for money.

1486
01:11:17,277 --> 01:11:19,571
We… [cries]

1487
01:11:20,322 --> 01:11:21,823
All right! Okay, okay.

1488
01:11:21,907 --> 01:11:23,534
Here, here. Take it.

1489
01:11:24,076 --> 01:11:25,827
Now, stop cryin', buddy.

1490
01:11:26,411 --> 01:11:28,038
Oh!

1491
01:11:29,706 --> 01:11:33,710
Um… Snake, what did you just do?

1492
01:11:33,794 --> 01:11:35,462
What? My friend was sad.

1493
01:11:35,546 --> 01:11:37,089
I was just cheerin' him up.

1494
01:11:37,172 --> 01:11:38,382
You…

1495
01:11:38,465 --> 01:11:40,384
You did a good thing. For me.

1496
01:11:40,467 --> 01:11:41,552
Don't be ridiculous.

1497
01:11:41,635 --> 01:11:43,971
I just put your needs before my own.

1498
01:11:44,054 --> 01:11:46,598
-Yeah. You're being good.
-I'm not.

1499
01:11:46,682 --> 01:11:49,643
I was simply making a sacrifice
so Shark could be happy.

1500
01:11:49,726 --> 01:11:52,563
That is the actual definition
of being good.

1501
01:11:52,646 --> 01:11:53,814
Snake!

1502
01:11:53,897 --> 01:11:55,691
You! The worst one of us!

1503
01:11:55,774 --> 01:11:57,901
-The most selfish.
-Spiteful.

1504
