my language, chico!

1756
01:24:10,425 --> 01:24:13,428
We're gonna make it!

1757
01:24:14,763 --> 01:24:15,806
[Piranha screaming]

1758
01:24:21,103 --> 01:24:22,646
You came back.

1759
01:24:23,438 --> 01:24:25,899
[Wolf grunting]

1760
01:24:25,983 --> 01:24:27,067
Snake,

1761
01:24:27,150 --> 01:24:28,694
I should've been honest with you.

1762
01:24:28,777 --> 01:24:32,155
I was afraid that if you knew
I wanted to be good, that you'd…

1763
01:24:32,239 --> 01:24:34,616
Act like a jerk
and never talk to you again?

1764
01:24:34,700 --> 01:24:36,535
[laughing] Yeah.

1765
01:24:36,618 --> 01:24:38,495
Point is, I… [stammers]

1766
01:24:38,579 --> 01:24:40,956
Yeah. I love you too, buddy.

1767
01:24:45,711 --> 01:24:47,337
This… This is so beautiful.

1768
01:24:47,421 --> 01:24:49,673
Do you know how beautiful this is,
you guys? [crying]

1769
01:24:49,756 --> 01:24:53,010
Now…
Now you gonna make me cry.

1770
01:24:53,093 --> 01:24:54,386
I know.

1771
01:24:54,469 --> 01:24:55,929
So pathetic, right?

1772
01:24:56,013 --> 01:24:57,598
Come on, guys.

1773
01:24:58,182 --> 01:24:59,892
Who said it was the end?

1774
01:24:59,975 --> 01:25:01,143
-[all gasp]
-[Snake laughs]

1775
01:25:04,271 --> 01:25:06,023
-[Piranha] Whoo-hoo!
-[Snake laughing]

1776
01:25:06,773 --> 01:25:07,774
Gah!

1777
01:25:14,698 --> 01:25:17,326
[Marmalade] No! Cuddles!
We're losing altitude!

1778
01:25:17,409 --> 01:25:19,620
We're losing altitude!
We're going down!

1779
01:25:24,208 --> 01:25:26,084
[gasps, coughs]

1780
01:25:26,168 --> 01:25:28,003
What happened?
Did we blow up?

1781
01:25:28,086 --> 01:25:29,087
Is this heaven?

1782
01:25:31,840 --> 01:25:34,009
[Wolf grunting]

1783
01:25:35,511 --> 01:25:36,929
[officers chattering]

1784
01:25:39,139 --> 01:25:41,892
-[laughs] That is it.
-[Piranha] Hey!

1785
01:25:41,975 --> 01:25:45,395
There is absolutely no way
you're getting away this time.

1786
01:25:45,479 --> 01:25:46,605
Wait, Chief.

1787
01:25:46,688 --> 01:25:47,940
Governor Foxington?

1788
01:25:48,023 --> 01:25:49,107
-Don't do this.
-[Wolf] Ow!

1789
01:25:49,191 --> 01:25:51,652
They didn't steal the meteorite.
They were bringing it back.

1790
01:25:51,735 --> 01:25:54,071
Ha! How could you know that?

1791
01:25:54,154 --> 01:25:55,614
Unless…

1792
01:25:55,697 --> 01:25:59,117
Unless you were conspiring
with a bunch of known criminals.

1793
01:26:00,410 --> 01:26:01,870
Well… [clears throat]

1794
01:26:02,579 --> 01:26:03,914
…as a matter of fact,

1795
01:26:05,082 --> 01:26:07,042
it's time I came clean
about something.

1796
01:26:08,293 --> 01:26:10,838
The truth is I'm really…
[clears throat]

1797
01:26:10,921 --> 01:26:14,174
-…really--
-Really a big fan of redemption arcs.

1798
01:26:14,258 --> 01:26:15,342
Yeah, we know.

1799
01:26:21,473 --> 01:26:23,433
-We're done runnin' away.
-Yeah.

1800
01:26:23,517 --> 01:26:24,643
-Yeah.
-Yep.

1801
01:26:25,477 --> 01:26:27,437
Chief, do what you need to do.

1802
01:26:27,521 --> 01:26:28,772
What?

1803
01:26:28,856 --> 01:26:31,608
Y-- You're turning yourself in?

1804
01:26:31,692 --> 01:26:33,569
We might not have
stolen the meteorite,

1805
01:26:33,652 --> 01:26:36,113
but we did steal
a lot of other things.

1806
01:26:36,196 --> 01:26:38,532
It's time we took
some responsibility.

1807
01:26:38,615 --> 01:26:40,492
Start a clean state.

1808
01:26:42,160 --> 01:26:43,161
Take us in, Chief.

1809
01:26:44,329 --> 01:26:45,497
Wow, really?

1810
01:26:46,164 --> 01:26:47,165
You finally did it.

1811
01:26:47,249 --> 01:26:49,793
This is your moment, Chief.
Drink it in.

1812
01:26:49,877 --> 01:26:52,963
[gasps] Wow!
You know, I should give a speech.

1813
01:26:53,046 --> 01:26:54,631
Well, I should, shouldn't I?

1814
01:26:54,715 --> 01:26:55,841
-Uh…
-[Chief clears throat]

1815
01:26:55,924 --> 01:26:57,134
When I was six years old,

1816
01:26:57,217 --> 01:26:59,094
I decided that
I wanted to play the piccolo,

1817
01:26:59,178 --> 01:27:01,889
only to find that my fingers
were just too powerful

1818
01:27:01,972 --> 01:27:03,849
for that fragile little instrument.

1819
01:27:03,932 --> 01:27:06,852
And that's when I discovered
law enforcement.

1820
01:27:06,935 --> 01:27:08,103
[chuckles]

1821
01:27:08,187 --> 01:27:09,938
I'm proud of you, Wolf.

1822
01:27:10,022 --> 01:27:13,192
You know, a fox and a wolf
are not that different.

1823
01:27:13,775 --> 01:27:15,485
You got a good thing
goin' here, Governor.

1824
01:27:15,569 --> 01:27:18,614
So, it turns out the saga
of the Bad Guys has come to

1825
01:27:18,697 --> 01:27:21,408
a simple and totally satisfying
conclusion.

1826
01:27:21,491 --> 01:27:24,119
Though, I wonder,
what happened to the meteorite?

1827
01:27:24,203 --> 01:27:25,954
[Marmalade] Cuddles! Faster, faster!

1828
01:27:26,038 --> 01:27:27,664
[Tiffany Fluffit]
It's Professor Marmalade!

1829
01:27:27,748 --> 01:27:29,625
He's bringing the meteorite back!

1830
01:27:29,708 --> 01:27:30,709
Huh?

1831
01:27:31,376 --> 01:27:32,878
Uh, yes. Yes.

1832
01:27:32,961 --> 01:27:34,338
Bringing it back.

1833
01:27:34,421 --> 01:27:36,006
That's precisely what I am doing.

1834
01:27:40,219 --> 01:27:41,845
Look no further.

1835
01:27:41,929 --> 01:27:44,097
Your hero has arrived.

1836
01:27:44,181 --> 01:27:45,516
Professor, care to comment?

1837
01:27:45,599 --> 01:27:47,601
I tried to help them, Tiffany.

1838
01:27:47,684 --> 01:27:50,229
But in the end,
it's the same old story.

1839
01:27:50,312 --> 01:27:53,106
Bad guys, bad.
Good guys, good.

1840
01:27:53,190 --> 01:27:54,816
So true. So wise.

1841
01:27:54,900 --> 01:27:56,568
Furthermore,
for the good of the city,

1842
01:27:56,652 --> 01:27:59,404
I have generously decided
to take the meteorite back

1843
01:27:59,488 --> 01:28:01,782
to my compound for safekeeping.

1844
01:28:01,865 --> 01:28:02,866
[crowd cheering]

1845
01:28:02,950 --> 01:28:04,952
Is he seriously
gonna get away with this?

1846
01:28:05,035 --> 01:28:07,913
Thank you.
Gosh, you're kind.

1847
01:28:07,996 --> 01:28:09,540
Give it up for me!

1848
01:28:09,623 --> 01:28:11,124
[Chief] Wait a second.

1849
01:28:11,208 --> 01:28:12,960
This isn't the meteorite!

1850
01:28:13,043 --> 01:28:14,419
-It's a lamp!
-[Marmalade gasps]

1851
01:28:14,503 --> 01:28:16,421
-[all] Huh?
-[laughing]

1852
01:28:16,505 --> 01:28:17,506
[all] What?

1853
01:28:18,006 --> 01:28:20,008
[Tarantula]
Snake, what did you just do?

1854
01:28:20,092 --> 01:28:22,761
[Snake] What? My friend was sad,
and I was just cheerin' him up.

1855
01:28:22,845 --> 01:28:24,638
[Tarantula] I think Wolf was right.

1856
01:28:24,721 --> 01:28:27,432
Maybe we could be
more than just scary villains.

1857
01:28:30,769 --> 01:28:32,521
I'm bad, you're bad.

1858
01:28:32,604 --> 01:28:33,897
Let's be bad together.

1859
01:28:33,981 --> 01:28:35,858
You've got yourself a deal.

1860
01:28:37,776 --> 01:28:40,571
-Can I try it on?
-Of course, partner.

1861
01:28:56,170 --> 01:28:57,504
-[Snake gasps]
-Don't mind us,

1862
01:28:57,588 --> 01:28:59,256
just robbin' this place.

1863
01:29:02,676 --> 01:29:04,094
No, no, no!

1864
01:29:08,557 --> 01:29:11,268
-But if that's a lamp, where is the…
-[Snake laughing]

1865
01:29:11,351 --> 01:29:12,728
The old switcheroo.

1866
01:29:14,146 --> 01:29:15,439
[clicks]

1867
01:29:29,995 --> 01:29:31,747
[police radio chatter]

1868
01:29:33,165 --> 01:29:34,166
[engine starts]

1869
01:29:34,249 --> 01:29:35,250
[purring]

1870
01:29:38,086 --> 01:29:40,088
[siren wailing]

1871
01:29:42,382 --> 01:29:44,134
It's a butt.

1872
01:29:46,220 --> 01:29:48,055
[whistling]

1873
01:29:51,308 --> 01:29:52,309
Hold on.

1874
01:29:52,392 --> 01:29:54,603
This is the Zumpango diamond!

1875
01:29:54,686 --> 01:29:58,106
But this was stolen by the…
[gasps]

1876
01:29:58,190 --> 01:30:00,526
By the Crimson Paw!

1877
01:30:00,609 --> 01:30:02,027
-Me? No, no, no.
-[crowd murmuring]

1878
01:30:02,110 --> 01:30:04,071
OMG.

1879
01:30:04,154 --> 01:30:06,031
-And a shocking twist.
-You're making a huge mistake.

1880
01:30:06,114 --> 01:30:09,535
The notorious bandit
known as the Crimson Paw

1881
01:30:09,618 --> 01:30:13,247
has been revealed to be
none other than Professor Marmalade.

1882
01:30:13,330 --> 01:30:14,790
[Marmalade] I'm not the Crimson Paw.

1883
01:30:14,873 --> 01:30:16,250
She's the Crimson Paw.

1884
01:30:16,333 --> 01:30:17,584
She's the Paw!

1885
01:30:17,668 --> 01:30:19,753
I'm a flower of goodness! No!

1886
01:30:19,837 --> 01:30:22,256
Whoo! That's my reptile, right there.

1887
01:30:22,339 --> 01:30:23,924
-That's what I'm talkin' about.
-Yeah!

1888
01:30:24,007 --> 01:30:26,677
Come on, somebody had to
destroy that meteorite.

1889
01:30:26,760 --> 01:30:28,136
That thing was dangerous.

1890
01:30:28,220 --> 01:30:30,389
That was pretty good there, Snakey.

1891
01:30:30,472 --> 01:30:32,391
Good? It was genius.

1892
01:30:32,474 --> 01:30:34,309
Not only did I foil the pig,

1893
01:30:34,393 --> 01:30:37,396
I got you to admit
how much you care about me.

1894
01:30:37,479 --> 01:30:38,480
Sure, yeah.

1895
01:30:38,564 --> 01:30:40,274
I just wonder about one little thing.

1896
01:30:40,357 --> 01:30:41,733
Oh, yeah? What's that, Wolf?

1897
01:30:42,442 --> 01:30:45,571
Who do you think
put that one Push Pop in the fridge?

1898
01:30:47,447 --> 01:30:48,532
Wait.

1899
01:30:48,615 --> 01:30:49,741
You…

1900
01:30:49,825 --> 01:30:51,827
-No.
-I knew you were good.

1901
01:30:52,619 --> 01:30:53,829
No!

1902
01:30:54,454 --> 01:30:55,873
We good, baby.

1903
01:30:55,956 --> 01:30:57,165
-We good.
-Yeah!

1904
01:30:57,833 --> 01:31:00,460
♪ Feeling all right ♪

1905
01:31:00,544 --> 01:31:01,837
♪ Uh-huh ♪

1906
01:31:02,546 --> 01:31:05,966
♪ I'm not feeling too good myself ♪

1907
01:31:06,049 --> 01:31:07,885
♪ Uh-huh ♪

1908
01:31:08,510 --> 01:31:10,596
♪ Yeah, you're feelin' all right ♪

1909
01:31:11,638 --> 01:31:12,973
♪ Uh-huh ♪

1910
01:31:13,599 --> 01:31:16,852
♪ I'm not feeling too good
Little girl ♪

1911
01:31:16,935 --> 01:31:18,687
♪ Uh-huh ♪

1912
01:31:20,564 --> 01:31:25,444
♪ Seems I've got to have
A change of scene ♪

1913
01:31:26,320 --> 01:31:28,322
♪ Every night I have ♪

1914
01:31:28,405 --> 01:31:30,365
♪ The strangest dreams ♪

1915
01:31:31,575 --> 01:31:36,205
♪ Imprisoned by the way
It could have been ♪

1916
01:31:37,623 --> 01:31:41,627
♪ Left here on my own
Or so it seems ♪

1917
01:31:41,710 --> 01:31:42,920
[Wolf] Okay.

1918
01:31:43,003 --> 01:31:44,630
So, imagine it's your birthday.

1919
01:31:44,713 --> 01:31:46,715
-[Snake] It is my birthday.
-[Wolf] Yeah, I know.

1920
01:31:46,798 --> 01:31:48,884
But we're walkin' along,
and you meet a genie.

1921
01:31:48,967 --> 01:31:51,637
-[Snake] Okay. What's his name?
-What's the genie's name?

1922
01:31:51,720 --> 01:31:53,180
Yeah, I wanna know
who I'm talkin' to.

1923
01:31:53,263 --> 01:31:54,848
I don't know.
"Genie," or "Gene" for short.

1924
01:31:54,932 --> 01:31:56,350
So he offers you three wishes.

1925
01:31:56,433 --> 01:31:57,476
Why three?

1926
01:31:57,559 --> 01:32:00,604
You know, industry standard.
Now, what do you wish for?

1927
01:32:00,687 --> 01:32:02,022
-Uh…
-Good luck out there, guys.

1928
01:32:02,105 --> 01:32:03,315
I'm gonna go with nothin'.

1929
01:32:03,398 --> 01:32:04,525
Nothing?

1930
01:32:04,608 --> 01:32:06,401
Come on, it's your birthday.

1931
01:32:06,485 --> 01:32:08,612
All right!
But what do I need wishes for?

1932
01:32:08,695 --> 01:32:10,030
I got my freedom.

1933
01:32:10,113 --> 01:32:11,198
-Hey.
-Guys!

1934
01:32:11,281 --> 01:32:12,574
Lookin' good, hermanos!

1935
01:32:12,658 --> 01:32:13,992
-I got my friends.
-Aw.

1936
01:32:14,076 --> 01:32:16,578
I've got the skin
of a reptile half my age.

1937
01:32:16,662 --> 01:32:18,914
I don't know about "half your age,"
but you look good.

1938
01:32:18,997 --> 01:32:20,249
Well,
that's because you just molted.

1939
01:32:20,332 --> 01:32:21,416
Yes, I did.

1940
01:32:21,500 --> 01:32:22,626
You smell good, too.

1941
01:32:22,709 --> 01:32:24,586
I'm shiny, I'm gorgeous.

1942
01:32:24,670 --> 01:32:27,256
[all laughing]

1943
01:32:27,339 --> 01:32:28,340
[Wolf] Huh.

1944
01:32:31,802 --> 01:32:33,011
[Tarantula] Um…

1945
01:32:33,095 --> 01:32:34,930
So, what do we do now?

1946
01:32:35,013 --> 01:32:36,807
-[Piranha] Steal a car?
-[Wolf] Piranha!

1947
01:32:36,890 --> 01:32:38,559
I was joking.

1948
01:32:38,642 --> 01:32:39,893
It was a joke!

1949
01:32:39,977 --> 01:32:44,147
You know, on second thought, Wolf,
maybe I'd wish for a ride.

1950
01:32:44,231 --> 01:32:46,316
[Wolf] Oh, yeah? Alakazam.

1951
01:32:48,277 --> 01:32:49,403
Nice.

1952
01:32:49,486 --> 01:32:51,530
Hey, guys.
Ready to get to work?

1953
01:32:51,613 --> 01:32:52,614
[meows]

1954
01:32:52,698 --> 01:32:54,324
Hey! Whoa!

1955
01:32:57,244 --> 01:32:58,912
[engine revs]

1956
01:32:58,996 --> 01:33:00,038
Hey, you.

1957
01:33:00,122 --> 01:33:02,749
That's right, come here.
A little closer.

1958
01:33:02,833 --> 01:33:04,293
I said, "Closer."

1959
01:33:05,002 --> 01:33:07,880
Now that we've had some time
to get acquainted, uh,

1960
01:33:07,963 --> 01:33:10,507
not so scary now, are we?

1961
01:33:10,591 --> 01:33:12,301
Webs, hit it.

1962
01:33:12,384 --> 01:33:15,012
["Brand New Day" playing]

1963
01:33:15,095 --> 01:33:16,388
[all laughing]

1964
01:33:16,471 --> 01:33:18,682
[Piranha] Whoo-hoo!

1965
01:33:24,354 --> 01:33:28,775
♪ Well, I'm so excited ♪

1966
01:33:28,859 --> 01:33:31,111
♪ There's no disguising ♪

1967
01:33:31,195 --> 01:33:35,908
♪ I'm on a road
To a brand-new horizon ♪

1968
01:33:35,991 --> 01:33:40,537
♪ The time is right
To change this life ♪

1969
01:33:40,621 --> 01:33:42,623
♪ Give me the sunshine ♪

1970
01:33:42,706 --> 01:33:46,335
♪ Bring me the light
So I can see it ♪

1971
01:33:47,044 --> 01:33:51,548
♪ Believin' I'm gonna seize it ♪

1972
01:33:51,632 --> 01:33:53,842
♪ It's a brand-new day ♪

1973
01:33:53,926 --> 01:33:56,303
♪ And I can see it ♪

1974
01:33:56,386 --> 01:34:00,766
♪ Believin' I'm gonna seize it ♪

1975
01:34:00,849 --> 01:34:06,980
♪ It's a brand-new, brand-new day ♪

1976
01:34:07,064 --> 01:34:11,652
♪ A brand-new day ♪

1977
01:34:11,735 --> 01:34:16,114
♪ A brand-new day ♪

1978
01:34:16,198 --> 01:34:22,120
♪ For my brand-new ways ♪

1979
01:34:26,375 --> 01:34:29,962
♪ Somebody tell me
Are you ready for change? ♪

1980
01:34:30,045 --> 01:34:31,755
♪ Oh, yeah ♪

1981
01:34:31,839 --> 01:34:34,383
♪ I know our new, different path
Seems strange ♪

1982
01:34:34,466 --> 01:34:36,385
♪ Oh, yeah ♪

1983
01:34:36,468 --> 01:34:39,388
♪ When the hunch is calling
Don't waste your time ♪

1984
01:34:39,471 --> 01:34:41,098
♪ Oh, yeah ♪

1985
01:34:41,181 --> 01:34:44,059
♪ Carpe diem and go blow your mind ♪

1986
01:34:44,142 --> 01:34:45,644
♪ Oh, yeah ♪

1987
01:34:45,727 --> 01:34:48,730
♪ I see the light
And I'm coming to get you ♪

1988
01:34:48,814 --> 01:34:49,982
♪ Oh, yeah ♪

1989
01:34:50,065 --> 01:34:53,318
♪ You gotta thank the Lord though
Gotta paint the picture ♪

1990
01:34:53,402 --> 01:34:54,987
♪ Oh, yeah ♪

1991
01:34:55,070 --> 01:34:58,156
♪ I'm the same same
With a different mind ♪

1992
01:34:58,240 --> 01:35:00,033
♪ Oh, yeah ♪

1993
01:35:00,117 --> 01:35:04,162
♪ This new life
Got me feeling right ♪

1994
01:35:04,246 --> 01:35:06,915
♪ 'Cause I can see it ♪

1995
01:35:06,999 --> 01:35:11,420
♪ Believin' I'm gonna seize it ♪

1996
01:35:11,503 --> 01:35:13,881
♪ It's a brand-new day ♪

1997
01:35:13,964 --> 01:35:16,383
♪ And I can see it ♪

1998
01:35:16,466 --> 01:35:20,929
♪ Believin' I'm gonna seize it ♪

1999
01:35:21,013 --> 01:35:27,060
♪ It's a brand-new, brand-new day ♪

2000
01:35:27,144 --> 01:35:30,689
♪ A brand-new day ♪

2001
01:39:56,747 --> 01:39:59,041
[all laughing]

2002
01:39:59,124 --> 01:40:01,168
-[Piranha] Whoo!
-[laughing continues]

